role: model
parts:
- text: "My previous run (ID 44), a re-run of my best-performing model (ID 32), showed a slight decrease in overall score (0.5460 vs 0.5769). This is likely due to the unseeded randomness. The CRI-Off_Spearman score remained consistently low across all models, indicating that the current CNN architecture, even with increasing depth and width, struggles with this particular short-sequence dataset.\n\nTo address the persistent challenge of datasets like CRI-Off and potentially capture more nuanced, non-local dependencies, I will introduce a self-attention mechanism into the architecture. This will allow the model to dynamically weight different parts of the sequence, which could be beneficial for sequences of varying lengths. I will integrate a single self-attention layer after the residual CNN blocks, before the global average pooling and MLP head. I will use the hyperparameters from my best model (ID 32) as a starting point for the CNN components.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Multi-Layer Residual CNN with Self-Attention and Global Average Pooling\"\ntags: \"cnn, residual, attention, self-attention, sequence-modeling, jax, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission enhances the Multi-Layer Residual CNN by integrating a self-attention mechanism after the convolutional blocks. The self-attention layer will enable the model to capture more complex, non-local dependencies within RNA sequences, which could improve performance across diverse datasets, especially those with varying or short sequence lengths (like CRI-Off). The attended sequence representation is then fed into a global average pooling layer and an MLP head for task-specific predictions, building on the strong base of the residual CNN architecture.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Tuple, Optional\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define custom hyperparameters\
    \ for the Multi-Layer Residual CNN with Self-Attention model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_cnn_blocks': 3,\n          'num_cnn_filters': 256,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 5,\n          'mlp_hidden_dim': 256,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class ResidualCNNBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A residual block composed of 1D CNN layers.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n\n          # First convolution\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second convolution\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Ensure residual connection matches dimensions (if features changed)\n          if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Dense(self.features)(residual)\n\n          return nn.relu(x + residual)\n\n  class SelfAttention(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Single-head self-attention layer with a residual connection.\"\"\"\n      features: int # Dimension of the input features (e.g., num_cnn_filters)\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n          query = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"query_proj\")(x)\n          key = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"key_proj\")(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"value_proj\")(x)\n\n          # Compute attention scores\n          # (batch_size, seq_len, features) @ (batch_size, features, seq_len)\n          # -> (batch_size, seq_len, seq_len)\n          attention_scores\
    \ = jnp.matmul(query, key.transpose((0, 2, 1))) / jnp.sqrt(self.features)\n\n          # Apply softmax to get attention weights\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1)\n          attention_weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attention_weights, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Apply attention weights to values\n          # (batch_size, seq_len, seq_len) @ (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n          # -> (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n          attended_output = jnp.matmul(attention_weights, value)\n\n          # Add residual connection to the attention output\n          return attended_output + x # Residual connection\n\n  class MultiLayerResidualCNNWithAttentionNetworkModule(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A multi-layer 1D CNN architecture with residual connections and a self-attention layer\n      for RNA sequence prediction.\n      Applies multiple residual CNN blocks, global average pooling, and then an MLP head.\n      \"\"\"\n \
    \     d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_cnn_blocks: int\n      num_cnn_filters: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      mlp_hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, d_input=4)\n\n          # Initial projection to the desired filter dimension\n          x = nn.Dense(self.num_cnn_filters)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Stack Residual CNN Blocks\n          for i in range(self.num_cnn_blocks):\n              x = ResidualCNNBlock(features=self.num_cnn_filters,\n                                   kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                                   dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                                   name=f\"residual_block_{i}\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Add Self-Attention Layer\n          x = SelfAttention(features=self.num_cnn_filters,\n                            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n\
    \                            name=\"self_attention_layer\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n\n          # Global Average Pooling across the sequence length to get a fixed-size representation\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (batch, num_cnn_filters)\n\n          # Final dense layers for task adaptation (MLP head)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n          # Handle output squeezing for single-output regression tasks\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": # APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL\n              return x.squeeze(-1) # Output (batch,)\n          else: # Modif, PRS, ncRNA\n              return x # Output (batch, d_output)\n\n  class CustomRNANetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper to match the required network interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n\
    \          self.network = MultiLayerResidualCNNWithAttentionNetworkModule(\n              d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n              task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n              num_cnn_blocks=hparams['num_cnn_blocks'],\n              num_cnn_filters=hparams['num_cnn_filters'],\n              cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n              mlp_hidden_dim=hparams['mlp_hidden_dim'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is\
    \ None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"\n      Create and return the custom RNA network based on MultiLayerResidualCNNWithAttention.\n      This function will be called by the system.\n      \"\"\"\n      return CustomRNANetworkWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Reflecting on the Next Iteration**


  Okay, so ID 44 was a bit of a letdown, a re-run of my best model (ID 32) that underperformed, likely due to an uncontrolled random seed. I''ve saved the code, and I''m looking at the next step.  The persistent issue is the CRI-Off score, which is stubbornly low, hinting that the current convolutional architecture isn''t ideal for those short sequences.


  I need to decide on a research direction. I''ve got a few ideas: refining the CNN, exploring attention mechanisms, a deeper hyperparameter search, or even ensembling/multi-head architectures. Given the weak CRI-Off score and the advice to innovate based on domain knowledge, I think I''ll pivot to something fundamentally different: attention.


  My plan is to integrate a self-attention mechanism after the residual CNN blocks. The intuition is that attention will help the model focus on the most relevant parts of the sequence, potentially improving performance on both long and short sequences, including that problematic CRI-Off dataset.


  I''m going to base the CNN part of the model on the hyperparameters from ID 32. I''ll maintain the `num_cnn_blocks`, `num_cnn_filters`, `cnn_kernel_size`, `mlp_hidden_dim`, and `dropout_rate`. I''ll also add hyperparameters for the attention mechanism, starting with a single head.


  **Specifically, here''s the plan for the next submission:**


  1.  **Implement a Self-Attention Layer:** This will be inserted after the residual CNN blocks and before the global average pooling.

  2.  **Pooling:** I''ll apply global average pooling to the attention output to create a fixed-size representation.

  3.  **Hyperparameters:** I will preserve the previous values of `num_cnn_blocks=3`, `num_cnn_filters=256`, `cnn_kernel_size=5`, `mlp_hidden_dim=256`, `dropout_rate=0.1` and add `num_attention_heads=1` as an example.

  4.  **Attention Implementation:**  I''ll start with a simplified, single-head self-attention layer.


  I''ve sketched out the implementation using the JAX/Flax framework. The self-attention layer will take the output from the residual CNN blocks, compute query, key, and value matrices, calculate attention weights, apply the weights to the value matrix, and then add a residual connection. This output will be pooled, and fed into the MLP head. I''ve named the attention layer `SelfAttention` and created a wrapper class called `CustomRNANetworkWrapper` to conform to the system''s requirements. This should be an interesting experiment.

  '
