tick: 30
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully saved the code for my stable baseline. My next step is to submit a new version of the Multi-Layer Residual CNN that incorporates a hybrid pooling strategy. This will involve concatenating the outputs of both Global Average Pooling and Global Max Pooling after the CNN blocks, then feeding these combined features into the MLP head. I am also increasing the `mlp_hidden_dim` to 512 to handle the larger input feature vector from the concatenated pooling layers.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Multi-Layer Residual CNN with Hybrid Global Pooling (Avg+Max)\"\ntags: \"cnn, residual, pooling, hybrid-pooling, global-average, global-max, sequence-modeling, jax, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission introduces a hybrid global pooling strategy to the Multi-Layer Residual CNN. After the convolutional blocks, both Global Average Pooling and Global Max Pooling are applied in parallel, and their outputs are concatenated. This aims to leverage the strengths of\
    \ both pooling methods—capturing general feature presence (average) and salient feature detection (max)—to generate a richer, more comprehensive sequence representation. The MLP head's hidden dimension is increased to accommodate the larger concatenated input, aiming to improve overall performance, especially for tasks sensitive to specific motif detection.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Tuple, Optional\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define custom hyperparameters for the Multi-Layer Residual CNN with Hybrid Pooling.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_cnn_blocks': 3,\n          'num_cnn_filters': 256,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 5,\n          'mlp_hidden_dim': 512, # Adjusted for concatenated pooling features (2 * 256)\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class ResidualCNNBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\
    \"\"A residual block composed of 1D CNN layers.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n\n          # First convolution\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second convolution\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Ensure residual connection matches dimensions (if features changed)\n          if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Dense(self.features)(residual)\n\n          return nn.relu(x + residual)\n\n\n  class MultiLayerResidualCNNWithHybridPoolingNetworkModule(nn.Module):\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      A multi-layer 1D CNN architecture with residual connections, hybrid global pooling,\n      and then an MLP head for RNA sequence prediction.\n      \"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_cnn_blocks: int\n      num_cnn_filters: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      mlp_hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, d_input=4)\n\n          # Initial projection to the desired filter dimension\n          x = nn.Dense(self.num_cnn_filters)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Stack Residual CNN Blocks\n          for i in range(self.num_cnn_blocks):\n              x = ResidualCNNBlock(features=self.num_cnn_filters,\n                                   kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                                   dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                                   name=f\"residual_block_{i}\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \n          # Hybrid Pooling: Global Average Pooling and Global Max Pooling\n          avg_pool_features = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (batch, num_cnn_filters)\n          max_pool_features = jnp.max(x, axis=1)  # (batch, num_cnn_filters)\n\n          # Concatenate features\n          x = jnp.concatenate([avg_pool_features, max_pool_features], axis=-1) # (batch, 2 * num_cnn_filters)\n\n          # Final dense layers for task adaptation (MLP head)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n          # Handle output squeezing for single-output regression tasks\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": # APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL\n              return x.squeeze(-1) # Output (batch,)\n          else: # Modif, PRS, ncRNA\n              return x # Output (batch, d_output)\n\n  class CustomRNANetworkWrapper:\n\
    \      \"\"\"Wrapper to match the required network interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.network = MultiLayerResidualCNNWithHybridPoolingNetworkModule(\n              d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n              task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n              num_cnn_blocks=hparams['num_cnn_blocks'],\n              num_cnn_filters=hparams['num_cnn_filters'],\n              cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n              mlp_hidden_dim=hparams['mlp_hidden_dim'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n\
    \              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"\n      Create and return the custom RNA network based on MultiLayerResidualCNNWithHybridPooling.\n      This function will be called by the system.\n      \"\"\"\n      return CustomRNANetworkWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Implementing the Hybrid Pooling Strategy**


  Okay, so I''ve got my baseline model code safe and sound. Now it''s time to put my hybrid pooling strategy into action. The idea is to merge the strengths of both Global Average Pooling and Global Max Pooling. This should let me capture the full picture of the sequence data while also zeroing in on those crucial, standout features. This should be particularly beneficial for tricky datasets like CRI-Off, where identifying the key differentiating characteristics can be a real challenge. I''ll need to remember to double the `mlp_hidden_dim` to account for the concatenated outputs from the different pooling methods; otherwise I''ll run into dimensional issues pretty quickly. Fingers crossed this approach yields a noticeable performance boost.

  '
