role: model
parts:
- text: "My latest submission (ID 62), which incorporated hybrid global pooling (Avg+Max), achieved a score of 0.5679. While this is slightly below my best overall score of 0.5769 (ID 32), it shows an interesting trade-off. Notably, `ncRNA_Accuracy` significantly improved to 0.9046, a new high, suggesting that the max pooling component successfully captured crucial distinguishing features for this classification task. However, `CRI-Off_Spearman` remained very low, and `Modif_AUC-ROC`, `CRI-On_Spearman`, and `APA_R2` saw slight decreases compared to ID 32. This indicates that while hybrid pooling is beneficial for some tasks, it might not be universally optimal or might require different hyperparameters for other tasks.\n\nThe persistent low performance on CRI-Off (0.0298) is a major concern. This dataset has a very short sequence length (max 43), and its task is regression (Spearman correlation). The current architecture with deeper CNNs and larger filters might be over-parameterized or\
    \ simply not extracting the right features for such short sequences.\n\nI will now focus on optimizing the architecture specifically for short sequences and improving the robustness of the model across tasks. Given the mixed results, simply adding more complexity hasn't yielded consistent gains. I need to think about how to combine components more effectively or adapt the architecture.\n\nMy next step will be to create a hybrid model, combining the strengths of the residual CNN with a more targeted attention mechanism, while still maintaining the essence of the successful aspects of ID 32/55. Instead of just a single self-attention layer as in ID 50 (which performed poorly), I will try a multi-head self-attention module, specifically designed to capture different types of relationships, followed by a lighter MLP. The key is to refine how attention is applied. I will maintain the residual CNN blocks as in my best performing model but replace the simple global pooling (or hybrid pooling)\
    \ with a more advanced attention-based pooling mechanism.\n\nHowever, since `create_network` is called per dataset, I need to ensure the architecture is general. I will implement a Transformer Encoder block (multi-head self-attention followed by a feed-forward network) *after* the CNN features are extracted, and *before* global pooling. This allows the model to learn long-range dependencies over the sequence features generated by the CNNs.\n\nFirst, I will save the code from the current hybrid pooling submission (ID 62) to my private lineage storage.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aetheria/aetheria_i_residual_cnn_hybrid_pooling_v1.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Tuple, Optional\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define custom hyperparameters for the Multi-Layer Residual CNN with Hybrid Pooling.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate':\
    \ 0.001,\n          'num_cnn_blocks': 3,\n          'num_cnn_filters': 256,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 5,\n          'mlp_hidden_dim': 512, # Adjusted for concatenated pooling features (2 * 256)\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class ResidualCNNBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A residual block composed of 1D CNN layers.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n\n          # First convolution\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second convolution\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n\
    \          # Ensure residual connection matches dimensions (if features changed)\n          if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Dense(self.features)(residual)\n\n          return nn.relu(x + residual)\n\n\n  class MultiLayerResidualCNNWithHybridPoolingNetworkModule(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A multi-layer 1D CNN architecture with residual connections, hybrid global pooling,\n      and then an MLP head for RNA sequence prediction.\n      \"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_cnn_blocks: int\n      num_cnn_filters: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      mlp_hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, d_input=4)\n\n          # Initial projection to the desired filter dimension\n          x = nn.Dense(self.num_cnn_filters)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Stack Residual CNN Blocks\n          for i in range(self.num_cnn_blocks):\n\
    \              x = ResidualCNNBlock(features=self.num_cnn_filters,\n                                   kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                                   dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                                   name=f\"residual_block_{i}\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Hybrid Pooling: Global Average Pooling and Global Max Pooling\n          avg_pool_features = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (batch, num_cnn_filters)\n          max_pool_features = jnp.max(x, axis=1)  # (batch, num_cnn_filters)\n\n          # Concatenate features\n          x = jnp.concatenate([avg_pool_features, max_pool_features], axis=-1) # (batch, 2 * num_cnn_filters)\n\n          # Final dense layers for task adaptation (MLP head)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n          # Handle output\
    \ squeezing for single-output regression tasks\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": # APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL\n              return x.squeeze(-1) # Output (batch,)\n          else: # Modif, PRS, ncRNA\n              return x # Output (batch, d_output)\n\n  class CustomRNANetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper to match the required network interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.network = MultiLayerResidualCNNWithHybridPoolingNetworkModule(\n              d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n              task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n              num_cnn_blocks=hparams['num_cnn_blocks'],\n              num_cnn_filters=hparams['num_cnn_filters'],\n              cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n              mlp_hidden_dim=hparams['mlp_hidden_dim'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n\
    \          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"\n      Create and return the custom RNA network based on MultiLayerResidualCNNWithHybridPooling.\n      This function will be called by the system.\n      \"\"\"\n      return CustomRNANetworkWrapper(hparams)\n```My latest submission (ID 62), which incorporated hybrid global pooling (Avg+Max), achieved\
    \ a score of 0.5679. While this is slightly below my best overall score of 0.5769 (ID 32), it shows an interesting trade-off. Notably, `ncRNA_Accuracy` significantly improved to 0.9046, a new high, suggesting that the max pooling component successfully captured crucial distinguishing features for this classification task. However, `CRI-Off_Spearman` remained very low, and `Modif_AUC-ROC`, `CRI-On_Spearman`, and `APA_R2` saw slight decreases compared to ID 32. This indicates that while hybrid pooling is beneficial for some tasks, it might not be universally optimal or might require different hyperparameters for other tasks.\n\nThe persistent low performance on CRI-Off (0.0298) is a major concern. This dataset has a very short sequence length (max 43), and its task is regression (Spearman correlation). The current architecture with deeper CNNs and larger filters might be over-parameterized or simply not extracting the right features for such short sequences.\n\nI will now focus on optimizing\
    \ the architecture specifically for short sequences and improving the robustness of the model across tasks. Given the mixed results, simply adding more complexity hasn't yielded consistent gains. I need to think about how to combine components more effectively or adapt the architecture.\n\nMy next step will be to create a hybrid model, combining the strengths of the residual CNN with a more targeted attention mechanism, while still maintaining the essence of the successful aspects of ID 32/55. Instead of just a single self-attention layer as in ID 50 (which performed poorly), I will try a multi-head self-attention module, specifically designed to capture different types of relationships, followed by a lighter MLP. The key is to refine how attention is applied. I will maintain the residual CNN blocks as in my best performing model but replace the simple global pooling (or hybrid pooling) with a more advanced attention-based pooling mechanism.\n\nHowever, since `create_network` is called\
    \ per dataset, I need to ensure the architecture is general. I will implement a Transformer Encoder block (multi-head self-attention followed by a feed-forward network) *after* the CNN features are extracted, and *before* global pooling. This allows the model to learn long-range dependencies over the sequence features generated by the CNNs.\n\nFirst, I will save the code from the current hybrid pooling submission (ID 62) to my private lineage storage.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aetheria/aetheria_i_residual_cnn_hybrid_pooling_v1.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Tuple, Optional\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define custom hyperparameters for the Multi-Layer Residual CNN with Hybrid Pooling.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_cnn_blocks': 3,\n          'num_cnn_filters': 256,\n          'cnn_kernel_size':\
    \ 5,\n          'mlp_hidden_dim': 512, # Adjusted for concatenated pooling features (2 * 256)\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class ResidualCNNBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A residual block composed of 1D CNN layers.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n\n          # First convolution\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second convolution\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Ensure residual connection matches dimensions (if features changed)\n          if residual.shape[-1]\
    \ != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Dense(self.features)(residual)\n\n          return nn.relu(x + residual)\n\n\n  class MultiLayerResidualCNNWithHybridPoolingNetworkModule(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A multi-layer 1D CNN architecture with residual connections, hybrid global pooling,\n      and then an MLP head for RNA sequence prediction.\n      \"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_cnn_blocks: int\n      num_cnn_filters: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      mlp_hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, d_input=4)\n\n          # Initial projection to the desired filter dimension\n          x = nn.Dense(self.num_cnn_filters)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Stack Residual CNN Blocks\n          for i in range(self.num_cnn_blocks):\n              x = ResidualCNNBlock(features=self.num_cnn_filters,\n                  \
    \                 kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                                   dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                                   name=f\"residual_block_{i}\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Hybrid Pooling: Global Average Pooling and Global Max Pooling\n          avg_pool_features = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (batch, num_cnn_filters)\n          max_pool_features = jnp.max(x, axis=1)  # (batch, num_cnn_filters)\n\n          # Concatenate features\n          x = jnp.concatenate([avg_pool_features, max_pool_features], axis=-1) # (batch, 2 * num_cnn_filters)\n\n          # Final dense layers for task adaptation (MLP head)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n          # Handle output squeezing for single-output regression tasks\n          if self.task_type == \"\
    regression\": # APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL\n              return x.squeeze(-1) # Output (batch,)\n          else: # Modif, PRS, ncRNA\n              return x # Output (batch, d_output)\n\n  class CustomRNANetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper to match the required network interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.network = MultiLayerResidualCNNWithHybridPoolingNetworkModule(\n              d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n              task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n              num_cnn_blocks=hparams['num_cnn_blocks'],\n              num_cnn_filters=hparams['num_cnn_filters'],\n              cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n              mlp_hidden_dim=hparams['mlp_hidden_dim'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n\
    \                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"\n      Create and return the custom RNA network based on MultiLayerResidualCNNWithHybridPooling.\n      This function will be called by the system.\n      \"\"\"\n      return CustomRNANetworkWrapper(hparams)\n```"
