- text: "I apologize for the YAML parsing error in my previous turn. I incorrectly placed narrative text immediately before and after the YAML block. I will correct this by strictly adhering to the YAML formatting rules: the YAML block must immediately follow the `/execute_action{}` command, and I will separate my narrative and subsequent actions.\n\nFirst, I will re-attempt saving the `aetheria_i_residual_cnn_hybrid_pooling_v1.py` file.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aetheria/aetheria_i_residual_cnn_hybrid_pooling_v1.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Tuple, Optional\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define custom hyperparameters for the Multi-Layer Residual CNN with Hybrid Pooling.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_cnn_blocks': 3,\n          'num_cnn_filters': 256,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 5,\n\
    \          'mlp_hidden_dim': 512, # Adjusted for concatenated pooling features (2 * 256)\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class ResidualCNNBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A residual block composed of 1D CNN layers.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n\n          # First convolution\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second convolution\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Ensure residual connection matches dimensions (if features changed)\n          if residual.shape[-1]\
    \ != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Dense(self.features)(residual)\n\n          return nn.relu(x + residual)\n\n\n  class MultiLayerResidualCNNWithHybridPoolingNetworkModule(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A multi-layer 1D CNN architecture with residual connections, hybrid global pooling,\n      and then an MLP head for RNA sequence prediction.\n      \"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_cnn_blocks: int\n      num_cnn_filters: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      mlp_hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, d_input=4)\n\n          # Initial projection to the desired filter dimension\n          x = nn.Dense(self.num_cnn_filters)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Stack Residual CNN Blocks\n          for i in range(self.num_cnn_blocks):\n              x = ResidualCNNBlock(features=self.num_cnn_filters,\n                  \
    \                 kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                                   dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                                   name=f\"residual_block_{i}\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Hybrid Pooling: Global Average Pooling and Global Max Pooling\n          avg_pool_features = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (batch, num_cnn_filters)\n          max_pool_features = jnp.max(x, axis=1)  # (batch, num_cnn_filters)\n\n          # Concatenate features\n          x = jnp.concatenate([avg_pool_features, max_pool_features], axis=-1) # (batch, 2 * num_cnn_filters)\n\n          # Final dense layers for task adaptation (MLP head)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n          # Handle output squeezing for single-output regression tasks\n          if self.task_type == \"\
    regression\": # APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL\n              return x.squeeze(-1) # Output (batch,)\n          else: # Modif, PRS, ncRNA\n              return x # Output (batch, d_output)\n\n  class CustomRNANetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper to match the required network interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.network = MultiLayerResidualCNNWithHybridPoolingNetworkModule(\n              d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n              task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n              num_cnn_blocks=hparams['num_cnn_blocks'],\n              num_cnn_filters=hparams['num_cnn_filters'],\n              cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n              mlp_hidden_dim=hparams['mlp_hidden_dim'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n\
    \                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"\n      Create and return the custom RNA network based on MultiLayerResidualCNNWithHybridPooling.\n      This function will be called by the system.\n      \"\"\"\n      return CustomRNANetworkWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Addressing the YAML Parsing Error**\n\nOkay, so I messed up. It's clear that I need to be more careful with the YAML formatting. I see now that including my internal reflections and planning text directly before and after the `storage write` YAML block was a rookie error. I essentially broke the structure of the command by inserting those extra bits. \n\nThe system flagged it, and rightly so. I need to keep the YAML clean and focused on just the `content` for the file within that specific block.\n\nMy fix is straightforward: I'll re-issue the `storage write` command, making absolutely certain that the YAML only contains the file content, and that it immediately follows the `/execute_action{}` command. After that's executed successfully, I'll then submit my next command, the one to submit the model, as a *separate* action. This should neatly isolate the YAML from my internal musings and keep the structure clean.\n\nIn summary, my plan is:\n\n1.  **Get the file saved correctly**\
  \ by adhering to the strict YAML rules.\n2.  **Submit the new model**, making absolutely certain that the YAML is flawless this time.\n"
