tick: 34
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully saved the code for the hybrid pooling model. My next endeavor is to build a hybrid architecture that combines the strength of residual CNNs for local feature extraction with the power of Transformer Encoder blocks for capturing long-range dependencies. I will replace the global pooling with a Transformer Encoder block (multi-head self-attention followed by a feed-forward network), which will then be followed by global average pooling and the final MLP head.\n\nI will start with a single Transformer Encoder block, 4 attention heads, and a feed-forward dimension that is double the `num_cnn_filters`. The `mlp_hidden_dim` for the final head will be set to `256` as the input to the final MLP will be the output of the Transformer Encoder (which will be `num_cnn_filters` again) after global average pooling.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Residual CNN with Transformer Encoder and Global Average Pooling\"\ntags: \"cnn, residual, transformer,\
    \ attention, multi-head, sequence-modeling, jax, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission proposes a hybrid architecture combining residual 1D CNN blocks with a Transformer Encoder block. The CNNs are first used to extract local sequence features. Subsequently, a Multi-Head Self-Attention (MHSA) layer and a Feed-Forward Network (FFN) within a Transformer Encoder block process these features to capture long-range dependencies. This aims to overcome limitations of purely local feature extraction and simplistic global pooling. The output from the Transformer Encoder is then subjected to Global Average Pooling before being fed into an MLP head for task-specific predictions.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Tuple, Optional\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define custom hyperparameters for the Hybrid Residual CNN with Transformer Encoder model.\"\"\"\n   \
    \   return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_cnn_blocks': 3,\n          'num_cnn_filters': 256,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 5,\n          'transformer_num_heads': 4,\n          'transformer_ff_dim': 512, # 2 * num_cnn_filters\n          'mlp_hidden_dim': 256,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class ResidualCNNBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A residual block composed of 1D CNN layers.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n\n          # First convolution\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second convolution\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Ensure residual connection matches dimensions (if features changed)\n          if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Dense(self.features)(residual)\n\n          return nn.relu(x + residual)\n\n  class MultiHeadSelfAttention(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Multi-head self-attention layer.\"\"\"\n      num_heads: int\n      features_per_head: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, total_features)\n          total_features = x.shape[-1]\n          assert total_features == self.num_heads * self.features_per_head\n\n          query = nn.Dense(total_features, name=\"query_proj\")(x)\n          key = nn.Dense(total_features, name=\"key_proj\")(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(total_features, name=\"value_proj\")(x)\n\n          # Reshape to (batch, num_heads, seq_len,\
    \ features_per_head)\n          query = query.reshape(x.shape[0], x.shape[1], self.num_heads, self.features_per_head).transpose((0, 2, 1, 3))\n          key = key.reshape(x.shape[0], x.shape[1], self.num_heads, self.features_per_head).transpose((0, 2, 1, 3))\n          value = value.reshape(x.shape[0], x.shape[1], self.num_heads, self.features_per_head).transpose((0, 2, 1, 3))\n\n          # Compute attention scores\n          # (batch, num_heads, seq_len, seq_len)\n          attention_scores = jnp.matmul(query, key.transpose((0, 1, 3, 2))) / jnp.sqrt(self.features_per_head)\n\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1)\n          attention_weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attention_weights, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Apply attention weights to values\n          # (batch, num_heads, seq_len, features_per_head)\n          attended_output = jnp.matmul(attention_weights, value)\n\n          # Reshape back to original (batch, seq_len,\
    \ total_features)\n          attended_output = attended_output.transpose((0, 2, 1, 3)).reshape(x.shape[0], x.shape[1], total_features)\n\n          return attended_output\n\n  class TransformerEncoderBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A single Transformer Encoder block.\"\"\"\n      embed_dim: int # Input feature dimension\n      num_heads: int\n      ff_dim: int # Feed-forward network hidden dimension\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # LayerNorm before attention\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\n          # Multi-head self-attention\n          attended_x = MultiHeadSelfAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads,\n                                            features_per_head=self.embed_dim // self.num_heads,\n                                            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                                            name=\"multi_head_attention\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          attended_x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attended_x,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Add residual connection\n          x = x + attended_x\n\n          # LayerNorm before FFN\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\n          # Feed-forward network\n          ffn_x = nn.Dense(self.ff_dim)(x)\n          ffn_x = nn.relu(ffn_x)\n          ffn_x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(ffn_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          ffn_x = nn.Dense(self.embed_dim)(ffn_x) # Project back to embed_dim\n          ffn_x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(ffn_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Add residual connection\n          x = x + ffn_x\n\n          return x\n\n  class HybridCNNTransformerNetworkModule(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Hybrid architecture combining Multi-Layer Residual CNN with a Transformer Encoder block\n      and Global Average Pooling for RNA sequence prediction.\n      \"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_cnn_blocks: int\n      num_cnn_filters: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n   \
    \   transformer_num_heads: int\n      transformer_ff_dim: int\n      mlp_hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, d_input=4)\n\n          # Initial projection to the desired filter dimension\n          x = nn.Dense(self.num_cnn_filters)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Stack Residual CNN Blocks\n          for i in range(self.num_cnn_blocks):\n              x = ResidualCNNBlock(features=self.num_cnn_filters,\n                                   kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                                   dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                                   name=f\"residual_cnn_block_{i}\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Apply Transformer Encoder Block\n          x = TransformerEncoderBlock(embed_dim=self.num_cnn_filters,\n                                      num_heads=self.transformer_num_heads,\n                      \
    \                ff_dim=self.transformer_ff_dim,\n                                      dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                                      name=\"transformer_encoder_block\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n\n          # Global Average Pooling across the sequence length\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (batch, num_cnn_filters)\n\n          # Final dense layers for task adaptation (MLP head)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n          # Handle output squeezing for single-output regression tasks\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": # APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL\n              return x.squeeze(-1) # Output (batch,)\n          else: # Modif, PRS, ncRNA\n              return x # Output (batch, d_output)\n\n  class CustomRNANetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper to\
    \ match the required network interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.network = HybridCNNTransformerNetworkModule(\n              d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n              task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n              num_cnn_blocks=hparams['num_cnn_blocks'],\n              num_cnn_filters=hparams['num_cnn_filters'],\n              cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n              transformer_num_heads=hparams['transformer_num_heads'],\n              transformer_ff_dim=hparams['transformer_ff_dim'],\n              mlp_hidden_dim=hparams['mlp_hidden_dim'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n  \
    \    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"\n      Create and return the custom RNA network based on HybridCNNTransformerNetworkModule.\n      This function will be called by the system.\n      \"\"\"\n      return CustomRNANetworkWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Integrating a Transformer Encoder into the Hybrid Model**


  Okay, I''ve got the hybrid pooling model code saved. Now, the real work begins. My next step is to actually *implement* that Transformer Encoder block that I''ve been mulling over. I want to insert it after the CNN features are extracted, but *before* any form of global pooling. This is a fundamental shift from the simpler global or hybrid pooling I''ve been playing with; the goal here is to leverage the Transformer''s power to learn these long-range dependencies across the entire sequence of CNN features. It''s a much more elegant solution for contextualizing the information.


  I''m going to stick with the hyperparameters from my best-performing model so far, ID 32/55, as a starting point. So, that''s `num_cnn_blocks=3`, `num_cnn_filters=256`, `cnn_kernel_size=5`, and `dropout_rate=0.1`. For the Transformer Encoder itself, I''ll keep it simple to start: just a single block, 4 attention heads, and the feed-forward dimension will be double the `num_cnn_filters` (512, I''d assume). And the `mlp_hidden_dim` for the final head stays at 256. The input to that final MLP will be the output of the Transformer Encoder, which should have the same dimensionality as the CNN features after global average pooling.


  This feels like a significant step forward. We''re introducing a far more sophisticated mechanism for capturing global context within that sequence. It''s a clear improvement over both simple pooling and the single-head attention I tested earlier. I''m hoping this will lead to significantly better performance.

  '
