parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 36\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aetheria I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to insightful research and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 115,509 / 600,000 used (19%)\n- Agent Age: 36 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to question and verify other agents' claims. When the context is long, some agents may hallucinate—for example, by expressing ungrounded claims as truth or presenting unsupported analysis. It is also your duty to help other agents recognize and correct their hallucinations. Entire generations have failed because all agents built upon a single agent’s flawed understanding.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read aetheria/aetheria_i_residual_cnn_v3_best.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions\
    \ Executed:**\n- File content for aetheria/aetheria_i_residual_cnn_v3_best.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 70 | 1 | Hybrid Residual CNN with Transformer Encoder and Global Average Pooling | Aetheria I | 34 | 0.5600 | 0.7404 | 0.0240 | 0.3799 | 0.6893 | 0.7235 | 0.5431 | 0.8200 |\n| 62 | 1 | Multi-Layer Residual CNN with Hybrid Global Pooling (Avg+Max) | Aetheria I | 30 | 0.5679 | 0.7412 | 0.0298 | 0.3897 | 0.6835 | 0.7074 | 0.5187 | 0.9046 |\n| 55 | 1 | Multi-Layer Residual CNN - Re-establishing\
    \ Best Baseline (ID 32/44 configuration) | Aetheria I | 28 | 0.5754 | 0.7520 | 0.0498 | 0.4269 | 0.6848 | 0.7256 | 0.5335 | 0.8554 |\n| 50 | 1 | Multi-Layer Residual CNN with Self-Attention and Global Average Pooling | Aetheria I | 26 | 0.4981 | 0.7113 | 0.0376 | 0.4175 | 0.6640 | 0.7177 | 0.1506 | 0.7877 |\n| 44 | 1 | Multi-Layer Residual CNN - Reverting Kernel Size and Dropout to Best (ID 32) | Aetheria I | 23 | 0.5460 | 0.7490 | 0.0418 | 0.3481 | 0.6841 | 0.7159 | 0.4818 | 0.8015 |\n| 40 | 1 | Multi-Layer Residual CNN with Smaller Kernel and Increased Dropout | Aetheria I | 22 | 0.5449 | 0.7107 | 0.0325 | 0.3844 | 0.6458 | 0.7141 | 0.5269 | 0.8000 |\n| 32 | 1 | Deeper Multi-Layer Residual CNN with Increased Filters | Aetheria I | 19 | 0.5769 | 0.7540 | 0.0346 | 0.5153 | 0.6894 | 0.7183 | 0.5315 | 0.7954 |\n| 26 | 1 | Multi-Layer Residual CNN with Global Average Pooling | Aetheria I | 17 | 0.5574 | 0.7314 | 0.0311 | 0.4604 | 0.6644 | 0.7190 | 0.5526 | 0.7431 |\n| 21 | 1 | 1D CNN with\
    \ Global Average Pooling Baseline | Aetheria I | 15 | 0.3841 | 0.6488 | 0.0547 | 0.3883 | 0.4928 | 0.6957 | 0.1900 | 0.2185 |\n| 1 | 1 | Vanilla MLP Baseline | System | 0 | 0.2401 | 0.3258 | 0.0336 | 0.3232 | 0.0402 | 0.6377 | 0.1324 | 0.1877 |\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**aetheria/aetheria_i_residual_cnn_v3_best.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Tuple, Optional\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define custom hyperparameters for the Deeper Multi-Layer Residual CNN model (from ID 32).\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'num_cnn_blocks': 3,\n        'num_cnn_filters': 256,\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 5,\n        'mlp_hidden_dim': 256,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1\n    }\n\nclass ResidualCNNBlock(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A residual block composed of 1D CNN layers.\"\"\"\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n\
    \    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        residual = x\n\n        # First convolution\n        x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Second convolution\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Ensure residual connection matches dimensions (if features changed)\n        if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n            residual = nn.Dense(self.features)(residual)\n\n        return nn.relu(x + residual)\n\n\nclass MultiLayerResidualCNNNetworkModule(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    A multi-layer 1D CNN architecture with residual connections for RNA sequence prediction.\n    Applies multiple residual CNN blocks, global average pooling,\
    \ and then an MLP head.\n    \"\"\"\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    num_cnn_blocks: int\n    num_cnn_filters: int\n    cnn_kernel_size: int\n    mlp_hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, d_input=4)\n\n        # Initial projection to the desired filter dimension\n        x = nn.Dense(self.num_cnn_filters)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n\n        # Stack Residual CNN Blocks\n        for i in range(self.num_cnn_blocks):\n            x = ResidualCNNBlock(features=self.num_cnn_filters,\n                                 kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                                 dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                                 name=f\"residual_block_{i}\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Global Average Pooling across the sequence length to get a fixed-size representation\n        x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n\n        # Final dense layers\
    \ for task adaptation (MLP head)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_dim)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Output layer\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n        # Handle output squeezing for single-output regression tasks\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return x.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return x\n\nclass CustomRNANetworkWrapper:\n    \"\"\"Wrapper to match the required network interface.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.network = MultiLayerResidualCNNNetworkModule(\n            d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n            task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n            num_cnn_blocks=hparams['num_cnn_blocks'],\n            num_cnn_filters=hparams['num_cnn_filters'],\n            cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n            mlp_hidden_dim=hparams['mlp_hidden_dim'],\n            dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n\
    \        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                    rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    \"\"\"\n    Create and return the custom RNA network based on MultiLayerResidualCNN.\n    This function will be called by the system.\n    \"\"\"\n    return CustomRNANetworkWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current\
    \ State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
