tick: 38
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have observed that my previous learning rate optimization attempt (ID 75) resulted in a score decrease, reinforcing that the original hyperparameters (from ID 32/55) provide the most stable baseline. The persistent low performance of CRI-Off suggests that the model is struggling to capture essential positional or short-range features for this dataset.\n\nTo address this, my next submission will enhance the robust Multi-Layer Residual CNN architecture with **fixed sinusoidal positional embeddings**. These embeddings will provide explicit positional information to the network, which is crucial for sequence-based tasks and is expected to particularly benefit datasets with shorter sequences or where order is highly important. I will inject these embeddings after the initial projection of the one-hot input and before the residual CNN blocks. I will revert the learning rate to `0.001` and maintain other hyperparameters from my best model (ID 32).\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Multi-Layer Residual CNN with Sinusoidal Positional Embeddings\"\ntags: \"cnn, residual, positional-encoding, sequence-modeling, jax, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission integrates fixed sinusoidal positional embeddings into the Multi-Layer Residual CNN architecture. The positional embeddings are added to the input sequence representation after its initial projection and before the convolutional layers. This aims to provide the model with explicit information about the relative or absolute position of nucleotides, which is hypothesized to improve feature learning, especially for datasets where sequence order is critical or sequence lengths are short (e.g., CRI-Off). All other hyperparameters are set to the values of the best-performing baseline (ID 32).\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Tuple, Optional\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define\
    \ custom hyperparameters for the Deeper Multi-Layer Residual CNN model with Positional Embeddings.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_cnn_blocks': 3,\n          'num_cnn_filters': 256,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 5,\n          'mlp_hidden_dim': 256,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_embedding_dim': 256 # Dimension for positional embeddings, matching num_cnn_filters\n      }\n\n  class PositionalEncoding(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, seq_len: int):\n          position = jnp.arange(seq_len, dtype=jnp.float32)[:, jnp.newaxis]\n          div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, self.d_model, 2, dtype=jnp.float32) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / self.d_model))\n          \n          pe = jnp.zeros((seq_len, self.d_model), dtype=jnp.float32)\n          pe = pe.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(position * div_term))\n          pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(position * div_term))\n\n          return pe\n\
    \n  class ResidualCNNBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A residual block composed of 1D CNN layers.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n\n          # First convolution\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second convolution\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Ensure residual connection matches dimensions (if features changed)\n          if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Dense(self.features)(residual)\n\n          return nn.relu(x + residual)\n\n\n\
    \  class MultiLayerResidualCNNWithPositionalEncodingNetworkModule(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A multi-layer 1D CNN architecture with residual connections,\n      fixed sinusoidal positional encoding, global average pooling, and an MLP head.\n      \"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_cnn_blocks: int\n      num_cnn_filters: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      mlp_hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      positional_embedding_dim: int # For the positional encoding\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, d_input=4)\n\n          # Ensure positional_embedding_dim matches num_cnn_filters for direct addition.\n          if self.positional_embedding_dim != self.num_cnn_filters:\n              raise ValueError(f\"positional_embedding_dim ({self.positional_embedding_dim}) must match num_cnn_filters ({self.num_cnn_filters}) for direct addition.\")\n          \n          # Initial projection\
    \ to the desired filter dimension\n          x = nn.Dense(self.num_cnn_filters)(x) # (batch, seq_len, num_cnn_filters)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Add Positional Encoding\n          current_seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          pe = PositionalEncoding(d_model=self.num_cnn_filters)(current_seq_len) # (current_seq_len, num_cnn_filters)\n\n          # Broadcast pe to match batch dimension\n          x = x + pe[jnp.newaxis, :, :] # (batch, seq_len, num_cnn_filters)\n\n          # Stack Residual CNN Blocks\n          for i in range(self.num_cnn_blocks):\n              x = ResidualCNNBlock(features=self.num_cnn_filters,\n                                   kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                                   dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                                   name=f\"residual_block_{i}\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Global Average Pooling across the sequence length to get a fixed-size representation\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n\
    \n          # Final dense layers for task adaptation (MLP head)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n          # Handle output squeezing for single-output regression tasks\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class CustomRNANetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper to match the required network interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.network = MultiLayerResidualCNNWithPositionalEncodingNetworkModule(\n              d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n              task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n              num_cnn_blocks=hparams['num_cnn_blocks'],\n              num_cnn_filters=hparams['num_cnn_filters'],\n              cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n\
    \              mlp_hidden_dim=hparams['mlp_hidden_dim'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              positional_embedding_dim=hparams['positional_embedding_dim'],\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\
    \"\"\n      Create and return the custom RNA network based on MultiLayerResidualCNNWithPositionalEncoding.\n      This function will be called by the system.\n      \"\"\"\n      return CustomRNANetworkWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Implementing Positional Embeddings for Short Sequences**


  My current best model, while decent, still struggles with the CRI-Off dataset, which has short sequences. I''ve been reading about how positional embeddings can help models understand the order of elements in sequences, and I think this could be the key to improving my results on CRI-Off.


  My plan is to add fixed sinusoidal positional embeddings to the input sequence before the CNN. I''ll start with the hyperparameters from my best-performing model (ID 32), and adjust things from there. Specifically, I''m going to project the positional embeddings to the same dimension as my CNN filters (`num_cnn_filters`) and add them to the output of the first dense layer in the CNN. I''ve built a `PositionalEncoding` module to handle this, which takes the sequence length as input. It will be added to the output of the first dense layer. I think this will work well as the input is now (batch, seq_len, num_cnn_filters), a well-defined format for the CNN. I have also adjusted the input argument to be `x` rather than explicit `seq_len` in the main module. I removed the `max_seq_len` argument. I''ve made sure to handle this in the `__call__` method. The output dimension of the positional embedding will match the output dimension of the initial projection from the input. I will need to test
  this, but based on my understanding this seems like a solid plan.

  '
