tick: 51
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully saved the code for my previous best baseline (ID 97 parameters). Now, having reviewed the approaches of other high-scoring agents, I will implement a significant architectural change inspired by their success: **Dilated Depthwise Separable Convolutions (DSConv)** within my residual blocks. This aims to increase the receptive field and capture multi-scale local patterns more efficiently, which might address the persistent challenges in tasks like CRI-Off.\n\nI will use a simpler CNN backbone (2 blocks, 128 filters, kernel 3) and retain the sinusoidal positional embeddings, as these elements contributed to my previous best performance. I'm introducing a `dilation_rate` of 2. For pooling, I will revert to Global Average Pooling to isolate the impact of the DSConvs.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Simpler Residual CNN with Positional Embeddings and Dilated Depthwise Separable Convolutions\"\ntags: \"cnn, residual, positional-encoding, dilated, depthwise-separable,\
    \ sequence-modeling, jax, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission enhances the current best-performing model by integrating Dilated Depthwise Separable Convolutions (DSConv) into the residual CNN blocks. This modification aims to increase the receptive field and capture multi-scale local patterns more efficiently, without significantly increasing model parameters. The architecture retains the simpler backbone (2 blocks, 128 filters, kernel 3) and sinusoidal positional embeddings from previous successful runs, followed by global average pooling and an MLP head. This is a targeted effort to improve feature extraction and potentially boost performance across all datasets, especially those with complex spatial dependencies and short sequence lengths like CRI-Off.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Tuple, Optional\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define custom\
    \ hyperparameters for the Simpler Residual CNN with Positional Embeddings and Dilated DSConvs.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_cnn_blocks': 2,\n          'num_cnn_filters': 128,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 3,\n          'dilation_rate': 2, # New hyperparameter for dilated convolution\n          'mlp_hidden_dim': 256,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_embedding_dim': 128 # Must match num_cnn_filters\n      }\n\n  class PositionalEncoding(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, seq_len: int):\n          position = jnp.arange(seq_len, dtype=jnp.float32)[:, jnp.newaxis]\n          div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, self.d_model, 2, dtype=jnp.float32) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / self.d_model))\n          \n          pe = jnp.zeros((seq_len, self.d_model), dtype=jnp.float32)\n          pe = pe.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(position * div_term))\n          pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(position\
    \ * div_term))\n\n          return pe\n\n  class DepthwiseSeparableConv1D(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A Flax implementation of Depthwise Separable Convolution 1D.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      strides: int = 1\n      padding: str = 'VALID'\n      dilation: int = 1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x: (batch, seq_len, in_features)\n          # Depthwise convolution\n          depthwise_conv = nn.Conv(\n              features=x.shape[-1], # Output features same as input features for depthwise\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              strides=(self.strides,),\n              padding=self.padding,\n              feature_group_count=x.shape[-1], # Group count = in_features for depthwise\n              name=\"depthwise_conv\",\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n              bias_init=nn.initializers.zeros(),\n              dilation=(self.dilation,) # Apply dilation here\n          )(x)\n  \
    \        \n          # Pointwise convolution\n          pointwise_conv = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.features, # Output features for pointwise\n              kernel_size=(1,),\n              strides=(1,),\n              padding='VALID',\n              name=\"pointwise_conv\",\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n              bias_init=nn.initializers.zeros()\n          )(depthwise_conv)\n          return pointwise_conv\n\n\n  class ResidualDSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A residual block composed of Dilated Depthwise Separable 1D CNN layers.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation_rate: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n\n          # First DSConv\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = DepthwiseSeparableConv1D(features=self.features,\n                                       kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n               \
    \                        dilation=self.dilation_rate, # Apply dilation\n                                       padding='SAME',\n                                       name=\"dsconv1\")(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second DSConv\n          x = DepthwiseSeparableConv1D(features=self.features,\n                                       kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                                       dilation=self.dilation_rate, # Apply dilation\n                                       padding='SAME',\n                                       name=\"dsconv2\")(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Ensure residual connection matches dimensions (if features changed)\n          if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Dense(self.features)(residual)\n\n          return nn.relu(x + residual)\n\n\n  class MultiLayerResidualDSConvWithPositionalEncodingNetworkModule(nn.Module):\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      A multi-layer Dilated Depthwise Separable CNN architecture with residual connections,\n      fixed sinusoidal positional encoding, global average pooling, and an MLP head.\n      \"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_cnn_blocks: int\n      num_cnn_filters: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      dilation_rate: int\n      mlp_hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      positional_embedding_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, d_input=4)\n\n          if self.positional_embedding_dim != self.num_cnn_filters:\n              raise ValueError(f\"positional_embedding_dim ({self.positional_embedding_dim}) must match num_cnn_filters ({self.num_cnn_filters}) for direct addition.\")\n          \n          # Initial projection to the desired filter dimension\n          x = nn.Dense(self.num_cnn_filters)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Add Positional\
    \ Encoding\n          current_seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          pe = PositionalEncoding(d_model=self.num_cnn_filters)(current_seq_len)\n          x = x + pe[jnp.newaxis, :, :]\n\n          # Stack Residual DSConv Blocks\n          for i in range(self.num_cnn_blocks):\n              x = ResidualDSConvBlock(features=self.num_cnn_filters,\n                                      kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                                      dilation_rate=self.dilation_rate, # Pass dilation rate\n                                      dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                                      name=f\"residual_dsconv_block_{i}\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Global Average Pooling across the sequence length to get a fixed-size representation\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n\n          # Final dense layers for task adaptation (MLP head)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class CustomRNANetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper to match the required network interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.network = MultiLayerResidualDSConvWithPositionalEncodingNetworkModule(\n              d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n              task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n              num_cnn_blocks=hparams['num_cnn_blocks'],\n              num_cnn_filters=hparams['num_cnn_filters'],\n              cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n              dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'], # Pass dilation rate\n              mlp_hidden_dim=hparams['mlp_hidden_dim'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              positional_embedding_dim=hparams['positional_embedding_dim'],\n\
    \          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"\n      Create and return the custom RNA network based on MultiLayerResidualDSConvWithPositionalEncodingNetworkModule.\n      This function will be called by the system.\n      \"\"\"\
    \n      return CustomRNANetworkWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analyzing Top Performers and Planning for Improvement**


  Okay, I''ve thoroughly reviewed the submissions from the top-performing agents. The results are striking. Models like Noema I and Veritas I are significantly outperforming my current best model. Their approaches are worth dissecting.


  A few key observations stand out. First, the "No-PE" tag is fascinating. It suggests their models extract information that inherently contains positional information, making explicit positional encoding less necessary. I''ve used positional encoding successfully in the past, but the success of these other models warrants revisiting its necessity. Secondly, "Dilated DSConv" is a prominent technique. The use of dilated depthwise separable convolutions is intriguing, as this allows for capturing features at multiple scales and expanding receptive fields efficiently. Veritas I''s combination of these with LSTMs and the use of "bilinear pooling" or "correlation pooling" mechanisms (like the "Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling" or "Offset Correlation Pooling" mentioned in Noema I) are also strong indicators of powerful techniques.


  My previous attempt at a self-attention layer didn''t pan out, showing that complex additions require careful integration. Considering the gains from these top-tier models, I will adopt a more iterative approach. Implementing dilated depthwise separable convolutions seems like a more manageable step than directly incorporating something like bilinear pooling right now. I''ll stick with global average pooling for this initial test to isolate the impact of the dilated convolutions.


  Therefore, the plan is to save my current best model (ID 97''s code) and then implement a new architecture. I will modify my residual CNN block to utilize Dilated Depthwise Separable Convolutions. I will keep the positional encoding for now, but I might do an ablation study on that later if results are positive. I''ll use parameters from ID 97 (re-run of ID 86), but introduce a new hyperparameter to specify the `dilation_rate` for the DSConvs. After making these modifications, I will submit the code with the relevant metadata.

  '
