parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 53\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aetheria I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to insightful research and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 193,587 / 600,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 53 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Simpler Residual CNN with Positional Embeddings and Dilated Depthwise Separable Convolutions' (ID: 103) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5072514981525946\n**APA_R2:** 0.7633\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0508\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9468\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.3691\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5057\n**MRL_R2:** 0.1474\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.7677\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 103\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed two critical bugs in the neural network implementation that were preventing code execution. The submission\
    \ now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had two Flax/JAX API usage errors in the `DepthwiseSeparableConv1D` class:\n\n1. **Incorrect initializer syntax**: Used `nn.initializers.zeros()` instead of `nn.initializers.zeros`\n   - In Flax, initializers should be passed as functions, not called\n   - The `zeros` initializer doesn't take arguments at instantiation time\n   - Error: `TypeError: zeros() missing 2 required positional arguments: 'key' and 'shape'`\n\n2. **Wrong parameter name for dilation**: Used `dilation=` instead of `kernel_dilation=`\n   - The `nn.Conv` layer in Flax uses `kernel_dilation` as the parameter name\n   - Error: `TypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'`\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (submission_v2.py)\nFixed the initializer syntax issue:\n```python\n# Before (lines 55, 62):\nbias_init=nn.initializers.zeros(),\n\n# After:\nbias_init=nn.initializers.zeros,\n```\n\nThis fix resolved the first error but\
    \ revealed the second issue.\n\n### Version 3 (submission_v3.py) - FINAL SUCCESS\nFixed the dilation parameter name:\n```python\n# Before (line 59):\ndilation=(self.dilation,)\n\n# After (line 59):\nkernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)\n```\n\nCombined with the initializer fix from v2, this allowed the code to run successfully.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitoring script confirmed the code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code 0 indicates successful execution\n- The neural network initialization and validation phases completed without errors\n\n## Technical Details\n- Fixed file: `submissions/submission_v3.py`\n- Affected class: `DepthwiseSeparableConv1D` (lines 47-68)\n- Total iterations: 3 versions (original → v2 → v3)\n- The fixes were simple API corrections that didn't change the algorithm's logic or architecture\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged\
    \ Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Tuple, Optional\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define custom hyperparameters for the Simpler Residual CNN with Positional Embeddings and Dilated DSConvs.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'num_cnn_blocks': 2,\n        'num_cnn_filters': 128,\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 3,\n        'dilation_rate': 2, # New hyperparameter for dilated convolution\n        'mlp_hidden_dim': 256,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_embedding_dim': 128 # Must match num_cnn_filters\n    }\n\nclass PositionalEncoding(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, seq_len: int):\n        position = jnp.arange(seq_len, dtype=jnp.float32)[:, jnp.newaxis]\n        div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, self.d_model, 2, dtype=jnp.float32) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / self.d_model))\n\
    \n        pe = jnp.zeros((seq_len, self.d_model), dtype=jnp.float32)\n        pe = pe.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(position * div_term))\n        pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(position * div_term))\n\n        return pe\n\nclass DepthwiseSeparableConv1D(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A Flax implementation of Depthwise Separable Convolution 1D.\"\"\"\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    strides: int = 1\n    padding: str = 'VALID'\n    dilation: int = 1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x: (batch, seq_len, in_features)\n        # Depthwise convolution\n        depthwise_conv = nn.Conv(\n            features=x.shape[-1], # Output features same as input features for depthwise\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            strides=(self.strides,),\n            padding=self.padding,\n            feature_group_count=x.shape[-1], # Group count = in_features for depthwise\n            name=\"depthwise_conv\",\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n\
    \            bias_init=nn.initializers.zeros,\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,) # FIXED: Changed from dilation to kernel_dilation\n        )(x)\n\n        # Pointwise convolution\n        pointwise_conv = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.features, # Output features for pointwise\n            kernel_size=(1,),\n            strides=(1,),\n            padding='VALID',\n            name=\"pointwise_conv\",\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n            bias_init=nn.initializers.zeros\n        )(depthwise_conv)\n        return pointwise_conv\n\n\nclass ResidualDSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A residual block composed of Dilated Depthwise Separable 1D CNN layers.\"\"\"\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation_rate: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        residual = x\n\n        # First DSConv\n        x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        x = DepthwiseSeparableConv1D(features=self.features,\n\
    \                                     kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                                     dilation=self.dilation_rate, # Apply dilation\n                                     padding='SAME',\n                                     name=\"dsconv1\")(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Second DSConv\n        x = DepthwiseSeparableConv1D(features=self.features,\n                                     kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                                     dilation=self.dilation_rate, # Apply dilation\n                                     padding='SAME',\n                                     name=\"dsconv2\")(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Ensure residual connection matches dimensions (if features changed)\n        if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n            residual = nn.Dense(self.features)(residual)\n\n   \
    \     return nn.relu(x + residual)\n\n\nclass MultiLayerResidualDSConvWithPositionalEncodingNetworkModule(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    A multi-layer Dilated Depthwise Separable CNN architecture with residual connections,\n    fixed sinusoidal positional encoding, global average pooling, and an MLP head.\n    \"\"\"\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    num_cnn_blocks: int\n    num_cnn_filters: int\n    cnn_kernel_size: int\n    dilation_rate: int\n    mlp_hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    positional_embedding_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, d_input=4)\n\n        if self.positional_embedding_dim != self.num_cnn_filters:\n            raise ValueError(f\"positional_embedding_dim ({self.positional_embedding_dim}) must match num_cnn_filters ({self.num_cnn_filters}) for direct addition.\")\n\n        # Initial projection to the desired filter dimension\n        x = nn.Dense(self.num_cnn_filters)(x)\n\
    \        x = nn.relu(x)\n\n        # Add Positional Encoding\n        current_seq_len = x.shape[1]\n        pe = PositionalEncoding(d_model=self.num_cnn_filters)(current_seq_len)\n        x = x + pe[jnp.newaxis, :, :]\n\n        # Stack Residual DSConv Blocks\n        for i in range(self.num_cnn_blocks):\n            x = ResidualDSConvBlock(features=self.num_cnn_filters,\n                                    kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                                    dilation_rate=self.dilation_rate, # Pass dilation rate\n                                    dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                                    name=f\"residual_dsconv_block_{i}\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Global Average Pooling across the sequence length to get a fixed-size representation\n        x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n\n        # Final dense layers for task adaptation (MLP head)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_dim)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Output layer\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return x.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return x\n\nclass CustomRNANetworkWrapper:\n    \"\"\"Wrapper to match the required network interface.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.network = MultiLayerResidualDSConvWithPositionalEncodingNetworkModule(\n            d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n            task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n            num_cnn_blocks=hparams['num_cnn_blocks'],\n            num_cnn_filters=hparams['num_cnn_filters'],\n            cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n            dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'], # Pass dilation rate\n            mlp_hidden_dim=hparams['mlp_hidden_dim'],\n            dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n            positional_embedding_dim=hparams['positional_embedding_dim'],\n        )\n\n    def init(self,\
    \ rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                    rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    \"\"\"\n    Create and return the custom RNA network based on MultiLayerResidualDSConvWithPositionalEncodingNetworkModule.\n    This function will be called by the system.\n    \"\"\"\n    return CustomRNANetworkWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution\
    \ Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation\
    \ works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 30572 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\n\
