tick: 72
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have saved the code for the precise Noema SOTA replication. My next step is to submit the new model using an \"Attention Pooling with Mean-Vector Query\" strategy, as inspired by Aletheia I's successful `CRI-Off` score in ID 111. This aims to find a pooling mechanism that performs better on `CRI-Off` while maintaining strong overall performance.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Noema Backbone with Mean-Vector Query Attention Pooling (No-PE)\"\ntags: \"cnn, dilated, depthwise-separable, attention, mean-query, no-positional-encoding, jax, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission integrates a novel attention pooling mechanism, where the global mean of sequence features serves as the query, into the Noema I-inspired Dilated DSConv backbone (No-PE). This \"Mean-Vector Query Attention Pooling\" replaces the previous hybrid pooling (Mean+MHA) to specifically address the persistently low performance on the CRI-Off task, while aiming to maintain overall high scores. The\
    \ architecture retains 5 residual blocks of dilated depthwise-separable 1D CNNs, GELU activations, and gradient clipping, with a targeted refinement in the pooling strategy.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n  # =========================\n  # Blocks and pooling\n  # =========================\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Pre-norm\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          # Depthwise conv (fixed: use kernel_dilation)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n\
    \              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h) # Using gelu as per Noema's SOTA\n          # Pointwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class AttentionPoolingWithMeanQuery(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Attention pooling layer where the query is the mean of sequence features.\"\"\"\n      features: int # Dimensionality of input features\n      attention_temperature: float = 1.0\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n          batch_size, seq_len, features = x.shape\n\n          # Compute the mean of sequence features to serve as the global query\n          mean_query = jnp.mean(x, axis=1, keepdims=True) # (batch, 1, features)\n\n          # Project keys from sequence elements\n      \
    \    keys = nn.Dense(features, use_bias=False, name=\"key_proj\")(x) # (batch, seq_len, features)\n\n          # Compute attention scores: (batch, 1, seq_len)\n          attention_scores = jnp.matmul(mean_query, keys.transpose((0, 2, 1))) / jnp.sqrt(features)\n          attention_scores /= self.attention_temperature\n\n          # Softmax over sequence length dimension to get weights\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1) # (batch, 1, seq_len)\n          attention_weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attention_weights, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Apply attention weights to values (x itself): (batch, 1, features)\n          attended_output = jnp.matmul(attention_weights, x)\n\n          # Squeeze the sequence length dimension (batch, features)\n          pooled_output = attended_output.squeeze(axis=1)\n\n          return pooled_output\n\n  # =========================\n  # Network\n  # =========================\n  class RNANetWithMeanQueryAttention(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, 4)\n          # Input projection\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Dilated DSConv stack\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model,\n                  kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                  dilation=d,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n    \
    \          )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Attention Pooling with Mean Query\n          pooled = AttentionPoolingWithMeanQuery(features=self.d_model,\n                                                  attention_temperature=self.attn_temp,\n                                                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Head - as per Noema's SOTA for consistent comparison\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class DSConvMeanQueryAttnNetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetWithMeanQueryAttention(d_input=d_input,\
    \ d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # =========================\n  # Station hooks\n  # =========================\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size':\
    \ 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'attn_temp': 0.5,\n          'positional_encoding': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return DSConvMeanQueryAttnNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          attn_temp=hparams.get('attn_temp', 0.5),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
