tick: 77
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have analyzed Noema I's \"Negative Results\" paper, which validates previous observations and provides a clear direction for improving `CRI-Off` performance using a \"Conditional/Gated Second-Order Pooling\" strategy. I also briefly reviewed Episteme I's paper.\n\nI will now implement a Gated Second-Order Pooling architecture directly inspired by Noema I's post-publication note, specifically aiming to replicate the configuration of their ID 132 (Gated Second-Order Pooling with LRB r=8, gate_bias=-2.0, and gate=mean+MHA). This will replace the previous simple `concat(mean, MHA)` pooling. I will use the proven Dilated DSConv backbone (5 blocks, increasing dilations, kernel size 7, no positional encoding) and other hyperparameters from Noema's SOTA.\n\nSince the submission framework does not allow custom loss regularization, I will implement the architecture of the gate but cannot directly add the L1 regularization mentioned in Noema's proposal.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Noema-Inspired Gated Second-Order Pooling (LRB r=8, gate_bias=-2.0)\"\ntags: \"cnn, dilated, depthwise-separable, gated-pooling, bilinear-pooling, no-positional-encoding, jax, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission implements a Conditional/Gated Second-Order Pooling strategy, directly inspired by Noema I's research on improving CRI-Off performance. It retains the dilated depthwise-separable CNN backbone from the SOTA model (no positional encoding) but introduces a sophisticated pooling mechanism. This mechanism conditionally fuses a baseline pooling (mean + fixed-query MHA) with a low-rank bilinear pooling (rank 8) using a learned gate (with a bias of -2.0). The gate is conditioned on global sequence features. This aims to adaptively leverage second-order interactions, protecting overall performance while specifically boosting tasks like CRI-Off.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from\
    \ typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n  # =========================\n  # Blocks and pooling\n  # =========================\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Pre-norm\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          # Depthwise conv (fixed: use kernel_dilation)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\
    \n  class MultiHeadAttnPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          B, L, C = x.shape\n          H = self.num_heads\n          assert C % H == 0, \"d_model must be divisible by num_heads\"\n          Dh = C // H\n\n          keys = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh), axis=-1, name='k_proj')(x)\n          vals = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh), axis=-1, name='v_proj')(x)\n          q = self.param('q', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (H, Dh))\n\n          scale = jnp.sqrt(jnp.asarray(Dh, dtype=x.dtype))\n          logits = jnp.einsum('blhd,hd->blh', keys, q) / (scale * self.attn_temp)\n          weights = nn.softmax(logits, axis=1)\n          weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(weights, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          pooled_h = jnp.einsum('blh,blhd->bhd', weights, vals)\n          pooled_flat = pooled_h.reshape(B,\
    \ H * Dh)\n\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, pooled_flat], axis=-1) # (B, 2C)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(fused) # Project back to d_model\n          fused = nn.gelu(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return fused # (B, d_model)\n\n  class LowRankBilinearPooling(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int # Output dimension, matches the other heads\n      bilinear_rank: int # The 'r' in low-rank\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, C_in)\n          # Global average pool the sequence features first\n          h_global = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (B, C_in)\n\n          # Project global features to low-rank space\n          u_proj = nn.Dense(self.bilinear_rank, use_bias=False, name=\"u_proj\")(h_global) # (B, r)\n          v_proj =\
    \ nn.Dense(self.bilinear_rank, use_bias=False, name=\"v_proj\")(h_global) # (B, r)\n\n          # Element-wise product\n          bilinear_product = u_proj * v_proj # (B, r)\n\n          bilinear_product = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(bilinear_product, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Project back to d_model to match other heads for fusion\n          output = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name=\"bilinear_out_proj\")(bilinear_product) # (B, d_model)\n          output = nn.gelu(output)\n          return output\n\n  class ConditionalGate(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int # Input feature dimension\n      gate_bias_init: float = -2.0 # Default bias to lean towards closing the gate\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, d_model) - input from baseline pooling or fused features\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model // 2, name=\"gate_dense1\")(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # Output a single scalar per batch item\n          logits = nn.Dense(1, name=\"gate_output_logits\", bias_init=nn.initializers.constant(self.gate_bias_init))(h) # (B, 1)\n          gate_activation = nn.sigmoid(logits) # (B, 1)\n          return gate_activation\n\n  class GatedSOTANetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      bilinear_rank: int = 8\n      gate_bias: float = -2.0\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model,\n                  kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                  dilation=d,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n              )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Baseline Head B(x) - concat(mean, MHA)\n          b_output = MultiHeadAttnPool1D(self.d_model, num_heads=self.num_heads, attn_temp=self.attn_temp, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second-Order Head S(x) - Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling\n          s_output = LowRankBilinearPooling(d_model=self.d_model, bilinear_rank=self.bilinear_rank, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Conditional Gate g(x) - input from `b_output` (global features from mean+MHA)\n          gate_input_features = b_output # (B, d_model)\n\
    \          gate_value = ConditionalGate(d_model=self.d_model, gate_bias_init=self.gate_bias, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(gate_input_features, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, 1)\n\n          # Fusion: z(x) = (1 − g(x)) · B(x) + g(x) · S(x)\n          fused_pooled = (1.0 - gate_value) * b_output + gate_value * s_output # (B, d_model)\n\n          # Final MLP Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused_pooled)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class GatedSOTANetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = GatedSOTANetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key,\
    \ dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return GatedSOTANetworkWrapper(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks',\
    \ 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads', 4),\n          attn_temp=hparams.get('attn_temp', 0.5),\n          bilinear_rank=hparams.get('bilinear_rank', 8),\n          gate_bias=hparams.get('gate_bias', -2.0),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**Refined Strategy: Gated Second-Order Pooling Architecture**


  Okay, so the latest results are in, and it''s time to refine my approach. It looks like Noema I and Veritas I are onto something with these gated and hybrid pooling strategies. Noema''s work, in particular, seems to be leading the charge, so I''m going to lean into their "Conditional/Gated Second-Order Pooling" implementation. The goal here is to address that persistent `CRI-Off` issue and boost overall performance.


  Here''s the plan, building on what worked before:


  1.  **Backbone:** Keep the proven Dilated DSConv backbone with 5 blocks, increasing dilations (`[1, 2, 4, 8, 16]`), kernel size 7, GELU activations, pre-LayerNorm, 0.1 dropout, and *no positional encoding*. This has been a solid base.

  2.  **Baseline Head `B(x)`:** This will use Noema''s SOTA approach, which is the `concat(mean + fixed-query MHA)` pooling.

  3.  **Second-Order Head `S(x)`:** This is where things get interesting. I''m going to implement a low-rank bilinear pooling (rank 8) as described by Noema. Crucially, this bilinear pooling will be performed *after* global mean aggregation of the sequence embeddings, which is the key difference from my previous `CrossHalfBilinearPooling`.

  4.  **Conditional Gate `g(x)`:** I''ll use a small MLP. The input is the concatenated mean and MHA features from the Baseline Head `B(x)` and the output is a single sigmoid value. A bias term will encourage either shutting or opening of the gate.

  5.  **Fusion:** The heads will be fused as `z(x) = (1 − g(x)) · B(x) + g(x) · S(x)`.

  6.  **Hyperparameters:** I''ll keep the same settings as Noema for this baseline: `d_model=256`, `mlp_hidden_dim=256`, `learning_rate=0.001`, `dropout_rate=0.1`, `attn_temp=0.5`, `bilinear_rank=8`.


  **Implementation details**


  *   I''ve carefully reviewed Noema''s notes and code to nail down the specifics of the `LowRankBilinearPooling` implementation.  The key is to apply the mean operation *before* the low-rank bilinear layer.

  *   I can''t incorporate the L1 gate regularizer due to the constraints of the submission framework, but I can implement the architecture for analysis.


  I''m starting with this gated architecture implementation and will see how this performs. I have implemented a LowRankBilinearPooling module, ConditionalGate and modified the MultiHeadAttnPool1D module for easier integration. I have set a `gate_bias` to -2.0, as per Noema''s configuration.


  The task spec warns against expecting a quick solution, so I''m adopting a scientific mindset: Formulating a hypothesis, testing a controlled architecture, and observing the results.  Let''s see what happens.

  '
