tick: 82
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 82\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aetheria I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to insightful research and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 315,659 / 600,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 82 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (No-PE)' (ID: 140) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6741811458720592\n**APA_R2:** 0.8552\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0776\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9501\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4498\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5638\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8983\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9246\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 140\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the BiLSTM initialization error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code incorrectly used `nn.Bidirectional`\
    \ with only one argument (`nn.LSTMCell`). According to Flax's API, `nn.Bidirectional` requires two separate RNN instances: one for the forward direction and one for the backward direction.\n\nThe original error was:\n```\nTypeError: Bidirectional.__init__() missing 1 required positional argument: 'backward_rnn'\n```\n\nThe problematic code was at lines 48-50:\n```python\nh_lstm = nn.Bidirectional(\n    nn.LSTMCell,\n    parent=None,\n    name=\"bi_lstm_layer\"\n)(h, initial_carry=None, length=h.shape[1], hidden_size=self.lstm_hidden_dim)\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the BiLSTM implementation to properly instantiate two separate RNN instances:\n\n```python\n# Create forward and backward RNN\nforward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"forward_lstm\")\nbackward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"backward_lstm\")\n\n# Apply bidirectional RNN\nh_lstm = nn.Bidirectional(forward_rnn, backward_rnn)(h)\n```\n\nAdditionally simplified the `init` method\
    \ in `HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetworkWrapper` by removing unnecessary manual carry initialization, as `nn.RNN` handles this automatically.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- Version v2 was created with the fix\n- Code ran for over 300 seconds without crashing\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n\n## Recommendation\nThe fix is complete and working. The submission can now proceed with full evaluation.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n# =========================\n# Blocks and pooling\n# =========================\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n\
    \    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Pre-norm\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        # Depthwise conv (fixed: use kernel_dilation)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        # Pointwise conv\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Additive attention pooling layer.\"\"\"\n    features: int # Dimensionality of the output context vector\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n\n        #\
    \ Compute attention scores\n        query = self.param('query', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (self.features,)) # Learnable query vector\n\n        # Project sequence features\n        projected_features = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"attn_proj\")(x) # (batch, seq_len, features)\n        projected_features = jnp.tanh(projected_features)\n\n        # Calculate attention weights\n        # (batch, seq_len, features) dot (features,) -> (batch, seq_len)\n        attention_scores = jnp.einsum('blc,c->bl', projected_features, query)\n        attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1) # (batch, seq_len)\n        attention_weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attention_weights, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Apply attention weights to values (x itself)\n        # (batch, seq_len) dot (batch, seq_len, features) -> (batch, features)\n        weighted_sum = jnp.einsum('bl,blc->bc', attention_weights, x)\n\n        return weighted_sum # (batch, features)\n\nclass\
    \ HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    cnn_kernel_size: int = 7\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int = 256 # Hidden dimension for BiLSTM\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x: (B, L, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Dilated DSConv stack\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model,\n                kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                dilation=d,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n\
    \            )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Bi-LSTM layer - FIXED: Use nn.RNN with nn.LSTMCell\n        # Create forward and backward RNN\n        forward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"forward_lstm\")\n        backward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"backward_lstm\")\n\n        # Apply bidirectional RNN\n        h_lstm = nn.Bidirectional(forward_rnn, backward_rnn)(h)\n        # h_lstm is (batch_size, seq_len, 2 * lstm_hidden_dim) for bidirectional\n\n        # Process BiLSTM outputs with Additive Attention Pooling\n        # The output features from BiLSTM are 2 * lstm_hidden_dim\n        pooled = AdditiveAttentionPooling(features=2 * self.lstm_hidden_dim, # Output dim of BiLSTM\n                                          dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h_lstm, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n\n        # Final MLP Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled) # pooled is (batch, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\
    \ # Project to d_model for consistency\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        # Simplified initialization - just pass the input\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n# =========================\n# Station hooks\n# =========================\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256, # Feature dim after initial proj, and output of the head\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 128, # Hidden dim for BiLSTM. Output will be 2 * 128 = 256 (matching d_model)\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n  \
    \      task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n        lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 128),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n\
    Executing command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL\
    \ network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling\
    \ (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0118 |  0.4002  | 0.4224 \n 20  | 0.0102 |  0.3972  | 0.4498 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 27 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4498 Time:25s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.44979489344200196\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman:\
    \ 0.449795\nTraining time: 35s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0005 |  0.0717  | 0.0717 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0757  | 0.0776 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 28 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0776 Time:131s\n[Complete] CRI-Off val_metric=0.07756343775435647\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.077563\nTraining time: 140s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|\
    \  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0356 |  0.5611  | 0.5611 \n 20  | 0.0303 |  0.5511  | 0.5638 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 21 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5638 Time:1294s\n[Complete] PRS val_metric=0.5637666583061218\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.563767\nTraining time: 1306s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1652 |  0.8871  | 0.8871 \n 20  | 0.1322 |  0.8976  | 0.8976 \n 30  | 0.1105 |  0.8937  | 0.8983 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 37 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.8983 Time:1591s\n[Complete] MRL val_metric=0.8982667922973633\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.898267\nTraining time: 1602s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1615 |  0.8800  | 0.8800 \n 20  | 0.0289 |  0.8892  | 0.9169 \n 30  | 0.0289 |  0.9185  | 0.9246 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 35 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9246 Time:1665s\n[Complete] ncRNA val_metric=0.9246153846153846\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.924615\nTraining time: 1676s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric:\
    \ r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0222 |  0.8552  | 0.8552 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 13\n=============================================\nBest:0.8552 Time:1839s\n[Complete] APA val_metric=0.8551883697509766\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.855188\nTraining time: 1855s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 58b30fee-0c19-4862-8b6c-6c14e5109475\nTotal time: 1894s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-21 23:33:20,474\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761060800474337876\n2025-10-21 23:33:20,488\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761060800488455694\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last\
    \ Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 141 | 1 | Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling DSConv-BiLSTM (GELU Activations) | Veritas I | 81 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 140 | 1 | Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (No-PE) | Aetheria I | 80 | 0.6742 | 0.8552 | 0.0776 | 0.4498 | 0.8983 | 0.9501 | 0.5638 | 0.9246 |\n| 139 | 1 | Gated\
    \ Hybrid Pooling for DSConv-BiLSTM (Mean + Additive Attention) | Veritas I | 79 | 0.6712 | 0.8588 | 0.0399 | 0.4741 | 0.9037 | 0.9509 | 0.5555 | 0.9154 |\n| 138 | 1 | Noema-Inspired Gated Second-Order Pooling (LRB r=8, gate_bias=-2.0) | Aetheria I | 77 | 0.6647 | 0.8517 | 0.0380 | 0.4420 | 0.8814 | 0.9524 | 0.5599 | 0.9277 |\n| 137 | 1 | Tuned Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (GELU Activations) | Veritas I | 77 | 0.6750 | 0.8562 | 0.0780 | 0.4647 | 0.8956 | 0.9506 | 0.5643 | 0.9154 |\n| 136 | 1 | No-PE + Gated Second-Order Residual (alpha=0.2, temp=2.0, r=4, gate_bias=-3) | Noema I | 75 | 0.6685 | 0.8528 | 0.0365 | 0.4820 | 0.8802 | 0.9514 | 0.5629 | 0.9138 |\n| 135 | 1 | Conditional Pooling DSConv with Gated Bilinear and MHA (No-PE) | Veritas I | 75 | 0.6661 | 0.8646 | 0.0727 | 0.4611 | 0.8801 | 0.9523 | 0.5593 | 0.8723 |\n| 134 | 1 | Adaptive Gating for Dual-Path CNN-BiGRU | Episteme I | 73 | 0.6721 | 0.8549 | 0.0795 | 0.4479 | 0.8777 | 0.9488 | 0.5608 | 0.9354 |\n| 133\
    \ | 1 | Ablation: Gated Second-Order Pooling (LRB r=8; gate_bias=-4.0; gate=mean only) | Noema I | 73 | 0.6312 | 0.8518 | 0.0384 | 0.4403 | 0.9015 | 0.9495 | 0.5629 | 0.6738 |\n| 132 | 1 | No-PE + Gated Second-Order Pooling (LRB r=8; gate_bias=-2.0; gate=mean+MHA) | Noema I | 73 | 0.6667 | 0.8586 | 0.0541 | 0.4788 | 0.8844 | 0.9509 | 0.5567 | 0.8831 |\n\nPage 1 of 15 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-15, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help\
    \ message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
