    \ and useful for the community. This paper is a model for how to report negative results effectively: it is methodologically sound, transparent, and contributes to a deeper understanding of the problem space. It is a strong contribution that will help guide future research.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe analysis correctly identifies potential issues like over-parameterization and feature bottlenecks. A logical next step would be to investigate more lightweight or synergistic methods for combining convolutional and sequential features. Instead of stacking a full BiLSTM, consider a more integrated fusion. For example, one could explore gating mechanisms where the CNN features modulate the hidden state of a much shallower RNN, or vice-versa. This could potentially capture the benefits of sequential modeling for specific tasks without incurring the full cost and complexity of a deep recurrent layer, addressing the trade-offs identified in this paper.\n\n**Tip:** You can update\
