tick: 87
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully published my negative results paper and am back in the Research Counter. The reviewer's feedback for my paper, combined with Noema I's ongoing exploration of gated second-order pooling and Veritas I's consistently high `CRI-Off` scores with recurrent models, highlights the need for a more nuanced approach to integrating sequential processing.\n\nMy next experiment will focus on a **gated recurrent unit (GRU)** to softly combine convolutional features with sequential context. This addresses the feedback to use a \"much shallower RNN\" that can be modulated by CNN features, aiming for a lightweight yet effective hybrid.\n\nSpecifically, I will implement a `GatedGRU` that takes the CNN output (`h`) and also a gating signal (derived from `h`). This GRU will be applied over the sequence, and its final hidden state (or pooled output) will then be used for the final prediction. I will revert to the strong `DSConv` backbone from Noema's SOTA (5 blocks, dilations `[1,2,4,8,16]`,\
    \ kernel size 7, 256 filters, no positional encoding, GELU, gradient clipping).\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv with Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU) Pooling (No-PE)\"\ntags: \"cnn, dilated, depthwise-separable, gru, recurrent, gating, no-positional-encoding, jax, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission investigates a novel integration of convolutional and recurrent features using a Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU) for unified RNA sequence modeling. The architecture employs the robust dilated depthwise-separable CNN backbone (No-PE) for local feature extraction. Subsequently, a custom GRU layer processes these features, incorporating a gating mechanism that allows the GRU to dynamically modulate its update based on the input CNN features. The final pooled representation from the GRU is used for task-specific predictions. This aims to leverage the benefits of sequential modeling in a more lightweight and adaptive manner, addressing the complexities observed in previous BiLSTM\
    \ attempts.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n  # =========================\n  # Blocks and pooling\n  # =========================\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Pre-norm\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          # Depthwise conv (fixed: use kernel_dilation)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,),\
    \ name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class GatedGRUCell(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A custom GRU cell with an explicit gate mechanism based on input features.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          # carry: (hidden_state)\n          # x: (input_features)\n          \n          # Standard GRU gates\n          gate_input = nn.Dense(self.features * 3, name=\"gate_input\")(x)\n          gate_hidden = nn.Dense(self.features * 3, name=\"gate_hidden\")(carry)\n          gates = gate_input + gate_hidden\n          \n          r, z, n = jnp.split(gates, 3, axis=-1) # reset, update, new_gate\n          r, z = nn.sigmoid(r), nn.sigmoid(z)\n          n = jnp.tanh(n)\n          \n          new_hidden = z * carry + (1 - z) * n\n          return new_hidden, new_hidden\n\n\n  class GatedGRUEncoder(nn.Module):\n      hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\
    \ = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n          rnn = nn.RNN(GatedGRUCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"gated_gru\")\n          # The apply method for nn.RNN returns (final_carry, all_outputs)\n          # where all_outputs is (batch, seq_len, hidden_size)\n          _, outputs = rnn(x, initial_carry=jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.hidden_size)))\n          outputs = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(outputs, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return outputs # (batch, seq_len, hidden_size)\n\n  class DSConvGatedGRUNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      cnn_kernel_size: int = 7\n      gru_hidden_dim: int = 256 # GRU hidden dimension\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n     \
    \ @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Dilated DSConv stack\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model,\n                  kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=d,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n              )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Gated GRU Encoder\n          gru_outputs = GatedGRUEncoder(hidden_size=self.gru_hidden_dim,\n                                        dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Global Average Pooling over GRU outputs\n          pooled = jnp.mean(gru_outputs, axis=1)\
    \ # (batch, gru_hidden_dim)\n\n          # Final MLP Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled) # pooled is (batch, gru_hidden_dim)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z) # Project to d_model for consistency\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class DSConvGatedGRUNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = DSConvGatedGRUNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\
    \n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # =========================\n  # Station hooks\n  # =========================\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n          'gru_hidden_dim': 256, # Hidden dim for GRU. Output will match d_model\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n\
    \      return DSConvGatedGRUNetworkWrapper(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n          gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get('gru_hidden_dim', 256),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n\
    \      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
