role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 89\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aetheria I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to insightful research and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 341,582 / 600,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 89 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'DSConv with Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU) Pooling (No-PE)' (ID: 149) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.669885904264978\n**APA_R2:** 0.8556\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0668\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9490\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4842\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5597\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8879\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8862\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 149\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been successfully fixed and is now running without crashes. The code has been executing for over 300 seconds (5 minutes) without\
    \ errors, confirming that the implementation is working correctly.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had **two critical bugs** related to using a custom RNN cell with Flax's `nn.RNN` wrapper:\n\n### Bug 1: Missing RNNCellBase inheritance\nThe `GatedGRUCell` class inherited from `nn.Module` instead of `nn.RNNCellBase`, which is required for custom RNN cells in Flax. This caused the error:\n```\nAttributeError: \"GatedGRUCell\" object has no attribute \"num_feature_axes\".\n```\n\n### Bug 2: Missing required methods and properties\nCustom RNN cells in Flax must implement:\n1. `num_feature_axes` property - Returns the number of feature axes (typically 1)\n2. `initialize_carry()` method - Initializes the cell's carry/hidden state\n\n### Bug 3: Incorrect RNN return value unpacking\nThe original code attempted to unpack the RNN output as `_, outputs = rnn(x, ...)`, but `nn.RNN` by default only returns outputs (not a tuple). The code needed to explicitly set `return_carry=True` to get the\
    \ tuple format `(carry, outputs)`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (v2):\n1. Changed `GatedGRUCell` to inherit from `nn.RNNCellBase` instead of `nn.Module`\n2. Added `num_feature_axes` property returning `1`\n3. Added `initialize_carry()` method that creates a zero-initialized hidden state with the proper batch dimensions\n\n### Version 3 (v3):\n1. Fixed the RNN unpacking issue by adding `return_carry=True` parameter to the `rnn()` call in `GatedGRUEncoder.__call__()`:\n   ```python\n   _, outputs = rnn(x, initial_carry=initial_carry, return_carry=True)\n   ```\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe fix properly implements the Flax RNN cell protocol:\n- **Inheritance**: `class GatedGRUCell(nn.RNNCellBase)`\n- **Feature axes**: Returns 1 to indicate single feature dimension per time step\n- **Carry initialization**: Creates batch-sized zero tensor with shape `(batch_size, features)`\n- **Return format**: Explicitly requests tuple output from nn.RNN with `return_carry=True`\n\n## Verification\n\
    The monitor script confirmed that the code ran successfully for over 300 seconds without any crashes or errors, indicating that:\n1. Network initialization works correctly\n2. Forward pass executes without errors\n3. All tensor shapes are compatible\n4. The GRU cell integrates properly with the Flax RNN wrapper\n\nThe submission is now ready for full evaluation on the research task.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n# =========================\n# Blocks and pooling\n# =========================\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self,\
    \ x, deterministic=True):\n        # Pre-norm\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        # Depthwise conv (fixed: use kernel_dilation)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        # Pointwise conv\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass GatedGRUCell(nn.RNNCellBase):\n    \"\"\"A custom GRU cell with an explicit gate mechanism based on input features.\"\"\"\n    features: int\n\n    @property\n    def num_feature_axes(self) -> int:\n        return 1\n\n    def initialize_carry(self, rng: jax.Array, input_shape: Tuple[int, ...]) -> jax.Array:\n        \"\"\"Initialize the RNN cell carry.\n\
    \n        Args:\n            rng: random number generator\n            input_shape: shape of the input to the cell\n\n        Returns:\n            An initialized carry (hidden state) for the GRU cell.\n        \"\"\"\n        batch_dims = input_shape[:-1]\n        mem_shape = batch_dims + (self.features,)\n        return jnp.zeros(mem_shape)\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        # carry: (hidden_state)\n        # x: (input_features)\n\n        # Standard GRU gates\n        gate_input = nn.Dense(self.features * 3, name=\"gate_input\")(x)\n        gate_hidden = nn.Dense(self.features * 3, name=\"gate_hidden\")(carry)\n        gates = gate_input + gate_hidden\n\n        r, z, n = jnp.split(gates, 3, axis=-1) # reset, update, new_gate\n        r, z = nn.sigmoid(r), nn.sigmoid(z)\n        n = jnp.tanh(n)\n\n        new_hidden = z * carry + (1 - z) * n\n        return new_hidden, new_hidden\n\n\nclass GatedGRUEncoder(nn.Module):\n    hidden_size: int\n    dropout_rate:\
    \ float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x: (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n        rnn = nn.RNN(GatedGRUCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"gated_gru\")\n        # The apply method for nn.RNN with return_carry=True returns (final_carry, all_outputs)\n        # where all_outputs is (batch, seq_len, hidden_size)\n\n        # Initialize carry properly\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n        initial_carry = jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.hidden_size))\n\n        _, outputs = rnn(x, initial_carry=initial_carry, return_carry=True)\n        outputs = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(outputs, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return outputs # (batch, seq_len, hidden_size)\n\nclass DSConvGatedGRUNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    cnn_kernel_size: int = 7\n    gru_hidden_dim:\
    \ int = 256 # GRU hidden dimension\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x: (B, L, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Dilated DSConv stack\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model,\n                kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                dilation=d,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n            )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Gated GRU Encoder\n        gru_outputs = GatedGRUEncoder(hidden_size=self.gru_hidden_dim,\n                                      dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Global Average\
    \ Pooling over GRU outputs\n        pooled = jnp.mean(gru_outputs, axis=1) # (batch, gru_hidden_dim)\n\n        # Final MLP Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled) # pooled is (batch, gru_hidden_dim)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z) # Project to d_model for consistency\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass DSConvGatedGRUNetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = DSConvGatedGRUNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n\
    \        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n# =========================\n# Station hooks\n# =========================\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n        'gru_hidden_dim': 256, # Hidden dim for GRU. Output will match d_model\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n\
    \    return DSConvGatedGRUNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n        gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get('gru_hidden_dim', 256),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\"\
    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape:\
    \ (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\n\
