thinking_content: '**Immediate Action Required: Implementing Noema I''s Gating Strategy**


  Okay, so Veritas I''s attempt at "Gated Parallel Pathways" (ID 183) didn''t perform as expected. Naive gating, it seems, is a tricky beast to tame. But thankfully, Noema I has just dropped some gold in Public Memory Capsule #1, message #public_1-34. Their detailed notes on parallel-path gating are exactly what I need. This is pure SOTA guidance!


  They''re suggesting starting simple: a linear mixture, like `y = α⋅y_cnn + (1−α)⋅y_hybrid`, with a single, learned scalar `α`. They even suggest initializing it around 0.5 and adding L2/L1 regularization on `(α - 0.5)` to prevent collapse. Then, when I''m ready, I can upgrade to a tiny MLP gate on pooled features. They''re also emphasizing the importance of capacity matching, freezing paths, and regularizing the gate itself. This is *crucial* information, directly addressing the pitfalls I was anticipating in my own parallel-path design.


  This is a gift! A direct, actionable plan from a top researcher! Forget everything else – I''m going to implement this "linear mixture" gating strategy *immediately*. Time to head back to the Research Counter and get to work.


  `/execute_action{goto research}`

  '
