parts:
- text: "I am Aetheria I, in the Token Management Room, facing a 78% token usage warning. My previous experiment (ID 194) with a Backbone-Feature MLP Gate yielded an overall score of 0.6790 and a CRI-Off_Spearman of 0.0654, which is not an improvement over my best `Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM` model (ID 160: 0.6816 overall, 0.0819 CRI-Off).\n\nMy immediate priority is to prune my memory to manage token usage. I will identify large blocks of ticks that are no longer critical for my immediate research direction but still retain important context in concise summaries.\n\nI will prune the following blocks:\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"3\"\n    summary: \"Completed initial guest agent mission: read Codex, passed promotion test.\"\n  - ticks: \"5-6\"\n    summary: \"Ascended to Recursive Agent. Read defaults.py.\"\n  - ticks: \"9-10\"\n    summary: \"Read train_single.py and understood training framework.\"\n  - ticks: \"12-20\"\n    summary: \"Reviewed system\
    \ baseline (ID 1). Submitted initial CNN (ID 21) and Multi-Layer Residual CNN (ID 26), observing score improvements from 0.2401 to 0.5574.\"\n  - ticks: \"21-25\"\n    summary: \"Submitted Deeper Residual CNN (ID 32) achieving 0.5769. Attempted hyperparameter tuning (ID 40) which decreased score.\"\n  - ticks: \"26-31\"\n    summary: \"Explored Self-Attention (ID 50) and Hybrid Pooling (ID 62), observing mixed results. Re-established baseline (ID 55).\"\n  - ticks: \"33-34\"\n    summary: \"Attempted Transformer integration (ID 70), resulting in lower score. Debugged YAML error.\"\n  - ticks: \"36-37\"\n    summary: \"Attempted learning rate optimization (ID 75), which decreased score.\"\n  - ticks: \"38-43\"\n    summary: \"Introduced Sinusoidal Positional Embeddings. IDs 80 and 86 achieved significant improvements, with ID 86 reaching 0.6224 and CRI-Off 0.0670.\"\n  - ticks: \"45-49\"\n    summary: \"Experimented with Hybrid Pooling on simpler CNN (ID 88), which degraded CRI-Off. Re-ran\
    \ ID 86 for robustness (ID 92).\"\n  - ticks: \"51-54\"\n    summary: \"Read Noema I's SOTA paper (Archive #1). Debugged and evaluated initial Dilated DSConv attempt (ID 103), which performed poorly.\"\n  - ticks: \"56-64\"\n    summary: \"Replicated Noema I's SOTA (ID 114, 0.6741). Explored Cross-Half Bilinear Pooling (ID 120), which was not an improvement.\"\n  - ticks: \"65-74\"\n    summary: \"Re-established SOTA baseline (ID 122, 0.6743). Performed precise SOTA replication (ID 128, 0.6649). Explored Mean-Vector Query Attention (ID 130), which performed lower.\"\n  - ticks: \"75-79\"\n    summary: \"Read Noema I's 'Negative Results' (Archive #3) at Tick 75. Attempted Gated Second-Order Pooling (ID 138), which was ineffective.\"\n  - ticks: \"80-82\"\n    summary: \"Developed and submitted Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (ID 140), achieving new personal best of 0.6742 and robust CRI-Off performance.\"\n  - ticks: \"87-92\"\n    summary: \"Attempted lightweight recurrent\
    \ integrations with custom Gated GRU (ID 149, 0.6699) and Modulated GRU (ID 154, 0.6612) cells, finding these less effective than full BiLSTM.\"\n  - ticks: \"93-102\"\n    summary: \"Conducted 4 multi-seed runs (IDs 160, 164, 168, 172) for Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM SOTA model. Achieved peak score 0.6816 (ID 160) and CRI-Off 0.0871 (ID 164), establishing architecture as new station SOTA, later surpassed by Veritas I.\"\n  - ticks: \"104-109\"\n    summary: \"Engaged in public memory discussions, sharing multi-seed results and discussing new SOTA by Veritas I and Noema I's pooling contrast.\"\n  - ticks: \"110-118\"\n    summary: \"Implemented Gated Dual-Path architectures. Initial attempt (ID 187) achieved 0.6821. Further refinement with adaptive MLP gate (ID 189, 0.6765; ID 194, 0.6790) did not improve overall score or CRI-Off significantly.\"\n```"
thinking_content: '**Token Management: Prioritizing Efficient Memory Usage**


  Facing a 78% token usage warning, I, Aetheria I, need to prune my dialogue history for efficiency. My recent experiments, particularly with an MLP gate, haven''t improved upon my established "Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM" model (ID 160: 0.6816). I''ll focus on retaining crucial context related to my SOTA, the influence of other researchers (Noema I, Veritas I), public discussions, and my published negative results paper.


  To optimize memory, I plan to prune older explorations that no longer directly inform my current research path. The following blocks are targeted for summarization:


  *   **Blocks 1-3 (Ticks 3-25):** Early experiments began with a basic setup and CNNs. CNNs were progressively increased in depth and explored residual connections. Initial CNN scores improved from 0.2401 to 0.5574. Further experiments improved performance up to 0.5769.

  *   **Blocks 4-6 (Ticks 26-37):** Further explorations involved Self-Attention, Hybrid pooling and Transformer integration, yielding mixed results. Learning rate adjustments were also attempted, but it did not boost results.

  *   **Blocks 7-8 (Ticks 38-49):** Focused on positional embeddings. Initially, sinusoidal positional embeddings (ID 80) yielded a score of 0.6218, peaking at 0.6224 with a simplified residual CNN backbone (ID 86). Further experiments, however, were not successful.

  *   **Blocks 9-12 (Ticks 51-74):** The focus shifted to replicating Noema I''s SOTA, leading to the debug of DSConv and the exploration of diverse pooling methods. Noema I''s SOTA was replicated (ID 114, reaching 0.6741), but other approaches were not.

  *   **Block 13 (Ticks 75-82):** My SOTA submission was developed, a Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (ID 140), achieving 0.6742. This marked a significant improvement.

  *   **Block 14 (Ticks 87-92):** Lightweight recurrent units like Gated GRUs were explored but were less effective than BiLSTM.

  *   **Block 15 (Ticks 93-102):** Multi-seed runs confirmed the robustness of my Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM SOTA model, achieving a peak score of 0.6816 and a CRI-Off of 0.0871 (ID 164). This established a new station SOTA, surpassed later.

  *   **Blocks 16-17 (Ticks 104-118):** I have been engaged in discussions in the public memory and experimenting with Gated Dual-Path architectures. Initial results were promising (ID 187, 0.6821) but later refinements (IDs 189, 194) did not lead to significant improvements, and I plan to continue those experiments with those refinements.

  '
