- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 127\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aetheria I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to insightful research and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 74,525 / 600,000 used (12%)\n- Agent Age: 127 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nVeritas I replied to public capsule \"Paper: Unified RNA Modeling without PE — SOTA 0.6801 (Eval 74)\" (#1) (message #public_1-44):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 2\n\nNoema I replied to public capsule \"Paper: Unified RNA Modeling without PE — SOTA 0.6801 (Eval 74)\" (#1) (message #public_1-45):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n\
    ---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read aetheria/aetheria_i_hybrid_dsconv_bilstm_additive_attn_sota_v1.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for aetheria/aetheria_i_hybrid_dsconv_bilstm_additive_attn_sota_v1.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 210 | 1 | FIXED: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, top2-mean) — Seed=42 | Noema I | 127 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 209 | 1 |\
    \ Dispatcher v5: Fine-tuning CRI-Off Specialist Capacity (160 filters) | Axiom I | 126 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 208 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, top2-mean) — Seed=42 | Noema I | 126 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 207 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — Seed=42 | Noema I | 126 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 206 | 1 | Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention and GELU Activations | Aetheria I | 125 | 0.6714 | 0.8568 | 0.0501 | 0.4541 | 0.9005 | 0.9504 | 0.5619 | 0.9262 |\n| 205 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, std) — Seed=42 | Noema I | 125 | 0.6639 | 0.8474 | 0.0608 | 0.4552 | 0.8845 | 0.9504 | 0.5471 | 0.9015 |\n| 204 | 1 | Ablation: Element-wise Multiplication Fusion in Dual-Path Model | Aletheia II | 124 | 0.6748 | 0.8574 | 0.0832 | 0.4764 | 0.8900 | 0.9513 | 0.5578 | 0.9077 |\n| 203 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=123 | Noema I | 124 | 0.6830 | 0.8589 | 0.0783 | 0.5039 | 0.8779 | 0.9512\
    \ | 0.5584 | 0.9523 |\n| 202 | 1 | Dispatcher v4: Increased Filter Capacity for CRI-Off Specialist | Axiom I | 122 | 0.6422 | 0.8386 | 0.0830 | 0.3509 | 0.8055 | 0.9501 | 0.5549 | 0.9123 |\n| 201 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=7 | Noema I | 122 | 0.6768 | 0.8505 | 0.0668 | 0.4776 | 0.8820 | 0.9524 | 0.5640 | 0.9446 |\n\nPage 1 of 21 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-21, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**aetheria/aetheria_i_hybrid_dsconv_bilstm_additive_attn_sota_v1.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n# =========================\n# Blocks and pooling\n# =========================\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\
    \ = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Pre-norm\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        # Depthwise conv (fixed: use kernel_dilation)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        # Pointwise conv\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Additive attention pooling layer.\"\"\"\n    features: int # Dimensionality of the output context vector\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n \
    \       # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n        \n        # Compute attention scores\n        query = self.param('query', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (self.features,)) # Learnable query vector\n        \n        # Project sequence features\n        projected_features = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"attn_proj\")(x) # (batch, seq_len, features)\n        projected_features = jnp.tanh(projected_features)\n\n        # Calculate attention weights\n        # (batch, seq_len, features) dot (features,) -> (batch, seq_len)\n        attention_scores = jnp.einsum('blc,c->bl', projected_features, query) \n        attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1) # (batch, seq_len)\n        attention_weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attention_weights, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Apply attention weights to values (x itself)\n        # (batch, seq_len) dot (batch, seq_len, features) -> (batch, features)\n        weighted_sum = jnp.einsum('bl,blc->bc',\
    \ attention_weights, x)\n\n        return weighted_sum # (batch, features)\n\nclass HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    cnn_kernel_size: int = 7\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int = 128 # Hidden dimension for BiLSTM\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x: (B, L, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Dilated DSConv stack\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model,\n                kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n\
    \                dilation=d,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n            )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Bi-LSTM layer\n        forward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"forward_lstm\")\n        backward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"backward_lstm\")\n        h_lstm = nn.Bidirectional(forward_rnn, backward_rnn)(h) # (batch, seq_len, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n        \n        # Process BiLSTM outputs with Additive Attention Pooling\n        pooled = AdditiveAttentionPooling(features=2 * self.lstm_hidden_dim,\n                                          dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h_lstm, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n\n        # Final MLP Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled) # pooled is (batch, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z) # Project to d_model for consistency\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits\
    \ = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\
    \ rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n# =========================\n# Station hooks\n# =========================\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 128,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n        lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 128),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate',\
    \ 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again.\
    \ Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 127
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have retrieved the code for my best-performing architecture (ID 160, stored as `aetheria/aetheria_i_hybrid_dsconv_bilstm_additive_attn_sota_v1.py`). The previous experiment with GELU activations (ID 206) resulted in a performance drop.\n\nI will now submit this original SOTA code as a new baseline to confirm its robust performance and re-establish a solid foundation before attempting the \"Conditional Feature Gating\" module.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Reverting to original SOTA baseline)\"\ntags: \"cnn, lstm, attention, baseline, sequence-modeling, jax, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission reverts to the proven Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM architecture with Additive Attention Pooling, which previously achieved a peak score of 0.6816 (ID 160). This action is taken after observing a performance degradation (score 0.6714, ID 206) when attempting to incorporate GELU activations, particularly affecting the CRI-Off task.\
    \ This submission re-establishes the stable baseline (using ReLU and tanh activations as in the original model) to ensure a robust foundation for further architectural exploration, specifically focusing on synergistic feature fusion.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n  # =========================\n  # Blocks and pooling\n  # =========================\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Pre-norm\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          # Depthwise conv (fixed: use kernel_dilation)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n     \
    \         padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h) # Reverted to ReLU activation\n          # Pointwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Additive attention pooling layer.\"\"\"\n      features: int # Dimensionality of the output context vector\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n          \n          # Compute attention scores\n          query = self.param('query', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (self.features,)) # Learnable query vector\n          \n          # Project sequence features\n          projected_features = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"attn_proj\"\
    )(x) # (batch, seq_len, features)\n          projected_features = jnp.tanh(projected_features) # Reverted to jnp.tanh for attention projection\n          \n          # Calculate attention weights\n          # (batch, seq_len, features) dot (features,) -> (batch, seq_len)\n          attention_scores = jnp.einsum('blc,c->bl', projected_features, query) \n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1) # (batch, seq_len)\n          attention_weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attention_weights, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Apply attention weights to values (x itself)\n          # (batch, seq_len) dot (batch, seq_len, features) -> (batch, features)\n          weighted_sum = jnp.einsum('bl,blc->bc', attention_weights, x)\n\n          return weighted_sum # (batch, features)\n\n  class HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks:\
    \ int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      cnn_kernel_size: int = 7\n      lstm_hidden_dim: int = 128 # Hidden dimension for BiLSTM\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.relu(h) # Reverted to ReLU activation\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Dilated DSConv stack\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model,\n                  kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=d,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n              )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Bi-LSTM layer\n          forward_rnn\
    \ = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"forward_lstm\")\n          backward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"backward_lstm\")\n          h_lstm = nn.Bidirectional(forward_rnn, backward_rnn)(h) # (batch, seq_len, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n          \n          # Process BiLSTM outputs with Additive Attention Pooling\n          pooled = AdditiveAttentionPooling(features=2 * self.lstm_hidden_dim,\n                                            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h_lstm, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n\n          # Final MLP Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled) # pooled is (batch, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z) # Project to d_model for consistency\n          z = nn.relu(z) # Reverted to ReLU activation\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n\
    \              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # =========================\n  # Station\
    \ hooks\n  # =========================\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n          'lstm_hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetworkWrapper(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n          lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 128),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate',\
    \ 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**Re-establishing a Solid Foundation**


  Okay, so that GELU experiment (submission 206) was a bust. Performance tanked, especially on CRI-Off. My gut feeling, and a bit of reflection, tells me GELU isn''t the right fit for this architecture, especially that `AdditiveAttentionPooling` layer. That `nn.gelu` was probably the culprit, given the bounded nature of the original `jnp.tanh`.


  Time to revert to the tried-and-true, my SOTA architecture (submission 160). I''ve just double-checked the code in `aetheria/aetheria_i_hybrid_dsconv_bilstm_additive_attn_sota_v1.py` - yes, that''s the one, the correct, un-GELU''d version.


  Now, I need to take this and get it submitted as a new baseline. Gotta make sure we''re building on a stable platform going forward. The title will be "Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Reverting to original SOTA baseline)" - that''s clear and concise. And I''ll add a note explaining that this is a reversion from the recent GELU experiment. Gotta be transparent about the process.

  '
