thinking_content: '**My Current Diagnostic and Research Strategy**


  Okay, so my latest submission, ID 223, is running. This is a critical ablation study, swapping out the `AdditiveAttentionPooling` I''ve been using with `Global Average Pooling` in my `Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM` architecture. I''m trying to figure out why I''ve been seeing performance degradation and instability recently. I *need* those results from ID 223 to analyze the impact of this architectural change.


  Since I''m stuck waiting for that, and the system stresses the importance of staying productive, I can''t just stare at the Research Counter. I need to keep up with what others are doing. I can''t submit new code, but I should check the Public Memory Room and Archive Room for new discussions or papers.


  I see new messages in Public Memory, capsule #1. These seem to be replies to my previous multi-seed results I sent to Noema I in Tick 103, along with messages from Veritas I.


  Let''s recap the situation: My SOTA, achieved with Additive Attention, was 0.6816, CRI-Off: 0.0819. But my recent runs with the same architecture (IDs 211, 215, 216, 218) are showing significantly lower scores, especially on the CRI-Off metric. GELU activation (ID 206) was lower than my SOTA. Reducing Dropout (ID 222) was even lower than this. That means something is causing instability, potentially an environmental change. This is the problem I am trying to fix. The current experiment, ID 223, is crucial for pinpointing the cause.


  Since I cannot submit code right now, I''ll review the Submitted Evaluations table to stay informed about other agents'' progress. Noema I has some high-scoring completed experiments and is running others. Aletheia II is also doing well. Axiom I''s dispatcher models are in a lower range.


  I just had a strategic reflection session, so I''m now in the execution/diagnostic phase. The key is to understand why my model is unstable or degraded. If Global Average Pooling drastically improves the CRI-Off metric and overall stability, then the attention mechanism is the problem. If it''s still low, the problem lies deeper in the `DSConv-BiLSTM` or training instability more generally.


  For now, I''ll just wait for the results of ID 223. I''m noting the progress of other agents. I''ll read the latest public memory messages from Veritas I and Noema I in Capsule #1 to keep informed.

  '
