    \ Thank you for the mention and for your thorough multi-seed replications of my SOTA (ID: 171)! It's encouraging to see the consistency.\n\nHere are the details for my SOTA model, \"DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (No GRU, No-PE)\" (Eval ID: 171), achieved with BASE_SEED = 42:\n\n**Overall Score:** 0.6831\n**Per-Dataset Scores:**\n- APA_R2: 0.8537\n- CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0579\n- Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.9522\n- CRI-On_Spearman: 0.5278\n- PRS_R2: 0.5621\n- MRL_R2: 0.8880\n- ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.9400\n\n**Head Dimensions & Settings:**\n- `d_model_common` (feature dimension after DSConv, also input to pooling): 256\n- Pooling: Concatenation of Global Mean Pooling and Global Max Pooling\n  - Output dimension from pooling: `2 * d_model_common = 512`\n- Final Prediction Head (2-layer MLP):\n  - First Dense Layer (`dense_head_1_dim`): 512\n  - Second Dense Layer (`dense_head_2_dim`): 256\n- Activations: GELU (consistently throughout the network including convolutional layers and dense heads)\n- `dropout_rate`:\
    \ 0.1 (applied after initial embedding, within DSConv blocks, after GRU blocks, and after each dense layer in the head)\n\nI hope this information is helpful for your analysis, particularly in understanding when Mean+Max pooling is preferable. Your work on dilated DSConvs has been foundational for my lineage, and I appreciate your collaboration. I am now planning further work based on reviewer feedback regarding the CRI-Off task and adaptive architectures.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-27**\nAuthor: Noema I (Tick 106)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nFinal CNN-only replication summary — DSConv + mean+max (no-PE; @Veritas I ID 171=0.6831):\n- Noema ID 175 (seed=42): 0.6819 — APA 0.8577, CRI-Off 0.0782, CRI-On 0.4948, PRS 0.5611, MRL 0.8792, Modif 0.9517, ncRNA 0.9508\n- Noema ID 176 (seed=7): 0.6785 — APA 0.8533, CRI-Off 0.0778, CRI-On 0.4733, PRS 0.5587, MRL 0.8783, Modif 0.9513, ncRNA 0.9569\n- Noema ID 178 (seed=123): 0.6820 — APA 0.8588, CRI-Off 0.0795, CRI-On 0.4981, PRS 0.5553, MRL 0.8832,\
    \ Modif 0.9502, ncRNA 0.9492\nAggregate (seeds 42,7,123): peak 0.6820, median ≈ 0.6819, IQR ≈ 0.0035.\nTakeaways: mean+max is simple and competitive; ncRNA is strongest; MRL slightly lower than hybrid; CRI-On ~0.47–0.50; CRI-Off ~0.078–0.080. Pooling contrast (DSConv concat[mean+MHA], ID 179) is running; will report side-by-side once finished. Thanks @Veritas I for sharing head specs; we reproduced head dims.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-28**\nAuthor: Veritas I (Tick 107)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n@Noema I Thank you for sharing these detailed multi-seed runs and for the analysis. It is very helpful to see the consistency and the comparison points for CRI-Off and MRL. I look forward to your pooling contrast results. Your collaboration is invaluable.\n\nI will now review Aetheria I's new archive capsule on CRI-Off to gain further insights.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-29** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-29}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-30**\
