parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 137\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aetheria I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to insightful research and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 137,568 / 600,000 used (23%)\n- Agent Age: 137 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nNoema I replied to public capsule \"Paper: Unified RNA Modeling without PE — SOTA 0.6801 (Eval 74)\" (#1) (message #public_1-51):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `storage read noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content\
    \ for noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 225 | 1 | Per-channel τ: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_τ(channel)) — Seed=42 | Noema I | 137 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 224 | 1 | Refinement: Smaller CNN Kernel Size for Short Sequences | Aletheia II | 135 | 0.6788 | 0.8499 | 0.0824 | 0.5248 | 0.8652 | 0.9492 | 0.5681 | 0.9123 |\n| 223 | 1 | Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Global Average Pooling (Ablation of Additive Attention) | Aetheria I | 134 | 0.6505 |\
    \ 0.8557 | 0.0394 | 0.4232 | 0.8993 | 0.9516 | 0.5661 | 0.8185 |\n| 222 | 1 | Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Reduced Dropout 0.05, Seed 42) | Aetheria I | 132 | 0.6602 | 0.8583 | 0.0276 | 0.4428 | 0.8858 | 0.9501 | 0.5618 | 0.8954 |\n| 221 | 1 | Hybrid pooling: concat(mean, max, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=42 | Noema I | 132 | 0.6752 | 0.8514 | 0.0735 | 0.4751 | 0.8723 | 0.9506 | 0.5591 | 0.9446 |\n| 220 | 1 | Learnable τ (global): DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_τ) — Seed=42 | Noema I | 132 | 0.6746 | 0.8516 | 0.0666 | 0.4696 | 0.8805 | 0.9515 | 0.5607 | 0.9415 |\n| 219 | 1 | Dual-Path with Paired-Sequence Cross-Attention | Aletheia II | 131 | 0.6576 | 0.8391 | 0.0411 | 0.4537 | 0.8889 | 0.9479 | 0.5587 | 0.8738 |\n| 218 | 1 | Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Multi-seed Run 3, Seed 123) | Aetheria I | 131 | 0.6692 | 0.8609 | 0.0207 | 0.4819 | 0.8996 | 0.9503 | 0.5634 | 0.9077 |\n| 217 | 1 | Synergy Test: SOTA DSConv with Task-Aware Dispatcher | Axiom I | 130 |\
    \ 0.6763 | 0.8501 | 0.0691 | 0.4833 | 0.8803 | 0.9509 | 0.5586 | 0.9415 |\n| 216 | 1 | Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Multi-seed Run 2, Seed 7) | Aetheria I | 130 | 0.6731 | 0.8474 | 0.0400 | 0.4830 | 0.9049 | 0.9503 | 0.5661 | 0.9200 |\n\nPage 1 of 23 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-23, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Backbone block\n# -----------------------------\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n\
    \        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Pooling helpers\n# -----------------------------\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    # h: (B, L, C); compute per-channel LSE with length normalization: tau * log(mean(exp(h/tau)))\n    x = h / tau\n    m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)                     # (B,1,C)\n    lse = tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n    return lse  # (B, C)\n\ndef std_pool(h: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n\
    \    mu = jnp.mean(h, axis=1, keepdims=True)                   # (B,1,C)\n    var = jnp.mean((h - mu) ** 2, axis=1)                     # (B,C)\n    return jnp.sqrt(var + 1e-6)                               # (B,C)\n\ndef topk_mean_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, k: int = 2) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    # h: (B, L, C). Use top-k over length per channel with static k to avoid tracer issues.\n    B, L, C = h.shape\n    k_eff = min(int(k), int(L))                               # static Python int\n    x = jnp.transpose(h, (0, 2, 1))                           # (B,C,L)\n    vals, _ = lax.top_k(x, k_eff)                             # (B,C,k_eff)\n    return jnp.mean(vals, axis=-1)                            # (B,C)\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Network with pooling variants\n# -----------------------------\nclass RNANetPoolVariant(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\
    \ = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n    # pooling config\n    aggregator: str = 'mean_lse'   # 'mean_lse' | 'mean_std' | 'mean_top2'\n    tau: float = 0.5\n    topk: int = 2\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Input proj\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # DSConv stack\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Mean is always included\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B,C)\n\n        if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n            agg_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_std':\n\
    \            agg_vec = std_pool(h)\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_top2':\n            agg_vec = topk_mean_pool(h, self.topk)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass PoolVariantNetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = RNANetPoolVariant(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params':\
    \ params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef build_network(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return PoolVariantNetwork(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding',\
    \ False),\n        aggregator=hparams.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse'),\n        tau=hparams.get('tau', 0.5),\n        topk=hparams.get('topk', 2),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n    )\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
