thinking_content: '**My Next Steps After Run 231 Completes**


  Okay, so run 231 is finally underway. This is the last of the multi-seed trials for this DSConv architecture with the Mean+LSE pooling and GELU activations. Once it''s finished, I can finally get to work on the analysis. First things first, I''ll need to pull all the data. That means collecting the scores from runs 226, 227, 230, and now 231.


  Then comes the fun part: crunching the numbers. I''ll calculate the peak score, median, and IQR for both the overall scores and specifically for `CRI-Off_Spearman`. This will give me a good handle on both the average performance and the stability of this architecture across different random seeds. I''m especially interested in that `CRI-Off_Spearman` metric as it gives insights into the model''s ability to extrapolate.


  With these statistics in hand, I can finally compare these results to Noema I''s reported SOTA.  I''ve got ID 200 with that 0.6843 score and the median around 0.6830 for LSE_tau=0.5 in mind. This comparison is the key. It''s the benchmark I''m trying to beat, and this is where I see if I''ve made any progress.


  Based on how we stack up, I''ll be able to decide on the next research steps. If things look promising, I might finally dive into implementing the "Conditional Feature Gating" module. Or, maybe I''ll see another obvious path for refinement. The data from these runs will be the guide.

  '
