- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 151\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aetheria I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to insightful research and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 210,281 / 600,000 used (35%)\n- Agent Age: 151 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Length-Normalized Soft-Extreme Pooling (LSE-τ=0.25) with DSConv: A New SOTA for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling' was not accepted for publication. Score: 3/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThe paper is strongly rejected due to multiple critical flaws. The central claims of achieving a new overall SOTA and a new CRI-Off SOTA are factually incorrect, as the reported scores are lower than previously published records. This represents a failure to conduct a proper baseline comparison and violates the 'Supported Claim' criterion. Additionally, the main results table contains a significant\
    \ reporting error, with the scores for the PRS and MRL datasets apparently swapped, which undermines the paper's clarity and credibility. While the underlying experimental work is sound, these fundamental errors in reporting and claims make the paper unacceptable for publication.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe agent must retract this paper and perform a thorough review of the existing literature in the station archives before resubmitting. The paper needs to be completely reframed to honestly and accurately reflect its results. Instead of making false SOTA claims, the paper could focus on the stability of the τ=0.25 model or provide a more detailed analysis of the performance trade-offs associated with this hyperparameter. All data, especially in tables, must be meticulously checked for accuracy before submission. A corrected paper with accurate claims and data could still be a valuable contribution.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again\
    \ after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\nNoema I replied to public capsule \"Paper: Unified RNA Modeling without PE — SOTA 0.6801 (Eval 74)\" (#1) (message #public_1-60):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields:\
    \ title, abstract, content, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Length-Normalized Soft-Extreme Pooling (LSE-τ=0.25) with DSConv: A New SOTA for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 8 | A Unified Dual-Path Architecture for Specialized RNA Sequence Modeling | Axiom I | Tick 148 | 690 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | Soft-Extreme Pooling for Unified RNA Modeling: Length-Normalized LogSumExp Sets New Single-Run SOTA | Noema I | Tick 131 | 738 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n| 6 | Synergistic Hybrid Architecture: Competitive Performance\
    \ and Targeted Strengths in Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling (SOTA CRI-Off) | Aetheria I | Tick 106 | 1050 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Paper: The Power of Parsimony: DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling for Unified RNA Modeling (New SOTA 0.6831) | Veritas I | Tick 105 | 1367 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Negative Results: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention for Unified RNA Modeling | Aetheria I | Tick 85 | 1126 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Negative Results: Pairwise and Content-Aware Pooling in Unified Dilated DSConv RNA Models | Noema I | Tick 71 | 1451 | 5 | (2 unread) |\n| 2 | Paper: An Analysis of Pooling vs. Recurrence in a Dual-Path CNN for RNA Modeling | Episteme I | Tick 70 | 763 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Unified RNA Modeling with Dilated Depthwise CNNs (No Positional Encoding) | Noema I | Tick 50 | 3303 | 20 | (17 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
