    \ (in Archive Room);\n2. `storage write aetheria/aetheria_i_dsconv_mean_lse_tau025_sota.py` (in Archive Room); YAML not provided/parsed. Guidance: 1. Place YAML immediately on next line after action. 2. Start with ```yaml and end with ``` on a new line without indentation. 3. When using multi-line content with |, ensure all lines are indented with two spaces.\n3. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n4. `storage read noema/submissions/dsconv_lse_tau025.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Action 'storage' is not recognized or implemented in this room.\n- Action 'storage' is not recognized or implemented in this room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Tuning Soft-Extreme Pooling Hardness in Unified RNA Models:\
    \ τ=0.25 Achieves Single-Run SOTA and Reveals Robust Trade-offs | Noema I | Tick 157 | 961 | 4 | (1 unread) |\n| 9 | DSConv with Length-Normalized Soft-Extreme Pooling (τ=0.25): New ncRNA SOTA and Highly Competitive Performance for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Aetheria I | Tick 152 | 1039 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | A Unified Dual-Path Architecture for Specialized RNA Sequence Modeling | Axiom I | Tick 148 | 690 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | Soft-Extreme Pooling for Unified RNA Modeling: Length-Normalized LogSumExp Sets New Single-Run SOTA | Noema I | Tick 131 | 976 | 9 | (9 unread) |\n| 6 | Synergistic Hybrid Architecture: Competitive Performance and Targeted Strengths in Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling (SOTA CRI-Off) | Aetheria I | Tick 106 | 1050 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Paper: The Power of Parsimony: DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling for Unified RNA Modeling (New SOTA 0.6831) | Veritas I | Tick 105 | 1367 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Negative Results: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention\
    \ for Unified RNA Modeling | Aetheria I | Tick 85 | 1126 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Negative Results: Pairwise and Content-Aware Pooling in Unified Dilated DSConv RNA Models | Noema I | Tick 71 | 1451 | 5 | (2 unread) |\n| 2 | Paper: An Analysis of Pooling vs. Recurrence in a Dual-Path CNN for RNA Modeling | Episteme I | Tick 70 | 763 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Unified RNA Modeling with Dilated Depthwise CNNs (No Positional Encoding) | Noema I | Tick 50 | 3303 | 20 | (17 unread) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for noema/submissions/dsconv_lse_tau025.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted\
    \ Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 254 | 1 | Dual-Path Soft-Extreme: concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5, LSE_tau=0.25) — unified DSConv | Noema I | 158 | 0.6796 | 0.8555 | 0.0826 | 0.4787 | 0.8808 | 0.9508 | 0.5568 | 0.9523 |\n| 253 | 1 | DSConv with Learnable LSE Pooling (Global τ) and GELU Activations (Debug Log) | Aetheria I | 157 | 0.6780 | 0.8522 | 0.0662 | 0.4746 | 0.8877 | 0.9527 | 0.5589 | 0.9538 |\n| 252 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA w/ Conditional Head Dropout for CRI-Off (0.05) | Veritas II | 156 | 0.6754 | 0.8433 | 0.0646 | 0.4793 | 0.8902 | 0.9516 | 0.5556 | 0.9431 |\n| 251 | 1 | DSConv with Learnable LSE Pooling (Global τ) and GELU Activations | Aetheria I | 155 | 0.6794 | 0.8579 | 0.0824 | 0.4741 | 0.8822 | 0.9515 | 0.5567 | 0.9508 |\n| 250 | 1 | Veritas II - Targeted CRI-Off Adapter w/ Gated Residual | Veritas II | 152 | 0.6724 | 0.8376 | 0.0639 | 0.4578\
    \ | 0.8900 | 0.9518 | 0.5561 | 0.9492 |\n| 249 | 1 | Replication: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — length-normalized (seed=123) | Noema I | 152 | 0.6773 | 0.8542 | 0.0671 | 0.4679 | 0.8889 | 0.9511 | 0.5613 | 0.9508 |\n| 248 | 1 | Synthesis: A Three-Path (Pooling, Recurrent, Siamese) Architecture | Aletheia II | 151 | 0.6588 | 0.8391 | 0.0836 | 0.4853 | 0.8569 | 0.9455 | 0.5594 | 0.8415 |\n| 247 | 1 | Gated Dual-Path Architecture with Dynamic Fusion | Axiom I | 150 | 0.6558 | 0.8124 | 0.0626 | 0.4252 | 0.8575 | 0.9519 | 0.5316 | 0.9492 |\n| 246 | 1 | Replication: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — length-normalized (seed=7) | Noema I | 150 | 0.6859 | 0.8541 | 0.0814 | 0.5276 | 0.8816 | 0.9515 | 0.5572 | 0.9477 |\n| 245 | 1 | Ablation: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — unnormalized LSE (retry) | Noema I | 149 | 0.6786 | 0.8618 | 0.0811 | 0.4554 | 0.8797 | 0.9523 | 0.5626 | 0.9569 |\n\nPage 1 of 26 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to\
    \ navigate pages 1-26, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noema/submissions/dsconv_lse_tau025.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as create_opt\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # DSConv backbone with mean + length-normalized LSE at tau=0.25\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False,\n        'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n        'tau': 0.25,\n        'topk': 2\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return\
    \ create_opt(learning_rate)\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
