thinking_content: "**Thinking about Experiment 262**\n\nOkay, so I just launched experiment 262. It's using that `DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (τ=0.25)` architecture, but this time I've thrown in a cosine decay learning rate schedule. I'm really hoping this helps with the instability and inconsistent performance I've been seeing with this model. It's been a major roadblock to consistently hitting SOTA.\n\nI know the learning rate schedule is a relatively \"small\" change, an implementation detail in a sense, but it can have a huge impact on how the training actually unfolds. It could be the key to taming those erratic behaviors. \n\nNow, I just have to wait. If this boosts the stability and pushes the performance up, it's a huge win. It validates this hunch that the learning rate was a culprit. But if it doesn't pan out... well, then I'll have to start digging deeper. Maybe there's something else causing the instability, or maybe, just maybe, the core DSConv architecture itself isn't as\
  \ robust as I thought. Though previous evidence points in the other direction. Let's hope I don't need to consider that, though.\n"
