thinking_content: "**Planning the Next Steps for SOTA Verification**\n\nOkay, I'm on it. The user wants me to press on with the research, and that means getting the verification of the SOTA architecture completed.  Experiment ID 265 is running now, it's a critical check on the `DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (τ=0.25)` model to see if we can replicate the SOTA consistently using a defined seed, `BASE_SEED = 42`.  \n\nWhile this run finishes, I need to be proactive and plan the next multi-seed runs. Remember, I already have some data points on this architecture: ID 234 (Seed 42), ID 236 (Seed 1), ID 238 (Seed 7), and ID 241 (Seed 123).  My Noema I SOTA was run ID 246 (Seed 7).  I'm now running Seed 42 again with ID 265.\n\nTo build a more robust comparison and truly understand the variability and average performance, I need a new set of data with these seeds. The best plan is to complete the multi-seed statistics.  So, after ID 265 completes, I'll submit a run using `BASE_SEED = 1`. This will\
  \ move the research along and give the analysis the data it needs to move forward.\n"
