tick: 175
role: model
parts:
- text: "My multi-seed SOTA re-verification runs are continuing to show inconsistent performance. The latest run (ID 268, Seed 1) achieved 0.6732, and the previous one (ID 265, Seed 42) achieved 0.6768. Both are significantly below the true SOTA (Noema I ID 246, 0.6859) and my own previous peak (ID 238, 0.6837) for this architecture. The `CRI-Off_Spearman` scores are particularly variable and often lower than expected.\n\nThis consistent inability to reproduce top performance reliably points to persistent instability in the training process for this specific `DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (tau=0.25)` architecture under current conditions. Simply re-running with different seeds is not resolving the core issue.\n\nTo address this, I need to systematically investigate the **training stability** of the model. I will focus on potential issues related to **gradient dynamics** and **optimization**. While `optax.adamw` with `clip_by_global_norm(1.0)` is generally robust, the aggressive nature of\
    \ `tau=0.25` pooling, especially for some datasets, might exacerbate gradient issues.\n\nMy next step is to conduct an ablation study on the `weight_decay` parameter in the `AdamW` optimizer. High weight decay can sometimes lead to instability or prevent the model from reaching good minima. I will reduce `weight_decay` from its current `0.01` to `0.001` and re-run the `DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (tau=0.25)` architecture with `BASE_SEED = 42`. This is a targeted attempt to improve training stability without altering the model architecture.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (τ=0.25) & Reduced Weight Decay (0.001)\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, lse, weight-decay, hyperparameter-tuning, stability, sequence-modeling, jax, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment investigates the impact of reducing the `weight_decay` parameter from 0.01 to 0.001 in the AdamW optimizer for the `DSConv with concat(mean, LSE_τ=0.25)` pooling architecture. Persistent performance\
    \ variability and suboptimal scores suggest training instability. This targeted hyperparameter adjustment aims to improve convergence stability, potentially allowing the model to achieve higher and more consistent performance, particularly for the challenging CRI-Off task. The model uses GELU activations and `BASE_SEED = 42`.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Backbone block\n  # -----------------------------\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n\
    \              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Pooling helpers\n  # -----------------------------\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      lse = tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n      return lse\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Network with pooling variants\n  # -----------------------------\n  class RNANetPoolVariant(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2,\
    \ 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      aggregator: str = 'mean_lse'\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      topk: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n              agg_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)\n\n\
    \          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class PoolVariantNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetPoolVariant(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # =========================\n  # Station hooks\n  # =========================\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'topk': 2,\n      }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.001) # MODIFIED: weight_decay reduced to 0.001\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED\
    \ = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
