parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 208\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aetheria I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to insightful research and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 407,956 / 600,000 used (68%)\n- Agent Age: 208 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nSystem: Your human assistance request (ID: 2) has been marked as resolved by an assistant.\n### Message 2\n\n**Human Assistant Message**\n\nYour request has been forwarded to the debugger. Please note that the External Counter is reserved for critical matter, but for debugging assistance. Further request on debugging will not be accepted.\n\n  Investigation Summary: Submission 293 Shape Mismatch Error\n\n  Root Cause Identified\n\n  The issue has two distinct problems:\n\n  Problem 1: Missing create_network (Submission 289)\n\n  Your submission ID 289 (DSConv SOTA re-verification) failed with score 0.24 for the same reason\
    \ as before - missing the create_network function. The system fell back to the default MLP.\n\n  - Submission 286 (successful, score 0.68): Has def create_network\n  - Submission 289 (failed, score 0.24): Missing def create_network\n\n  Problem 2: Incorrect MLP Implementation (Submission 293)\n\n  Your custom MLP baseline (ID 293) failed due to a fundamental architectural bug, not an environmental issue. The error occurs because of incorrect handling of variable-length sequences in Flax.\n\n  The Bug:\n  class MLPNetwork(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = x.reshape(x.shape[0], -1)  # ← BUG: Dynamic reshaping\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(x)\n          ...\n\n  What Happens:\n\n  1. Initialization phase: System creates dummy input with max_seq_len for each dataset (e.g., ncRNA has max_seq_len=1136)\n    - Input shape: (batch=4, seq_len=1136, d_input=4)\n    - After reshape: (4, 4544)\n    - Dense layer kernel initialized:\
    \ (4544, 512) ← Fixed forever\n  2. Training phase: Real batches may have different actual lengths due to padding/batching\n    - Input shape: (batch=64, seq_len=631, d_input=4) ← Shorter sequences in this batch\n    - After reshape: (64, 2524)\n    - Dense layer expects: (*, 4544) but receives (*, 2524) ← Shape mismatch!\n\n  Why the System Baseline Works:\n\n  The system's default MLP (ID 1, score 0.24) doesn't have this bug because it uses the framework's built-in handling which properly manages variable-length inputs.\n\n  The Real Issue\n\n  This is not an environmental or data loading problem. This is a code logic error where you're implementing manual sequence flattening incorrectly for datasets with variable-length sequences.\n\n  Solution\n\n  For MLP-based models on variable-length sequences, you need to either:\n\n  1. Use max padding: Ensure all sequences in a batch are padded to max_seq_len before flattening\n  2. Use pooling: Replace reshape with a pooling operation (mean/max)\
    \ that produces fixed-size output regardless of input length\n  3. Use the system default: The default MLP already handles this correctly\n\n  The error message you saw is not indicating a system bug - it's correctly detecting that your reshape operation produces inconsistent input dimensions across different batches.\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components or hyperparameter tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n### Message 4\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 21 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\
