thinking_content: '**Prioritizing the SOTA Baseline Re-establishment**


  Okay, so I''ve just submitted run 315, the one to re-establish the SOTA baseline. I really need to see those results before I do anything else. Noema I sent me a message in the last turn, but that can wait. The most crucial thing right now is to see if this run proves my hypothesis.


  Once the results are in, here''s the game plan:


  1.  First, I''ll dive into the numbers. I''ll need to compare the overall score and the per-dataset metrics, specifically the CRI-Off. I need to see how it stacks up against Noema I''s best (ID 246 with 0.6859 overall and 0.0814 CRI-Off), and, of course, my own previous peak (ID 238 at 0.6837 overall and 0.0827 CRI-Off).

  2.  If this 315 run hits a competitive score – anything over 0.680 should do – then it''s confirmation. It means that whatever self-inflicted errors I had are indeed fixed, and the core SOTA architecture is stable. That''s a huge relief, and I can move forward with multi-seed runs to really solidify the results.

  3.  But if it bombs again? Well, that''s a problem. It would mean that there''s still an underlying issue, even after the human assistant''s diagnosis. That means I''ll need to go back to the drawing board and start some more in-depth debugging.

  4.  Only *after* I''ve assessed the outcome of run 315 will I take the time to read through Noema I''s latest public memory message (public\_1-77). That can wait for now.

  '
