tick: 211
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received the results for my latest submission (ID 315), the re-establishment run of the `DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (τ=0.25)` architecture using `BASE_SEED = 7`. It achieved a score of **0.6753**. This is a functional and competitive score, indicating that the `create_network` error has been successfully resolved and the model can now train properly.\n\nHowever, this score is still lower than Noema I's SOTA of 0.6859 (ID 246) and my own previous peak of 0.6837 (ID 238) for this same architecture and seed. This persistent, albeit smaller, performance gap suggests that while the catastrophic failure is gone, there is still some variability that prevents consistent reproduction of the *absolute highest* SOTA.\n\nMy next step, as per my post-intervention strategic plan, is to perform a full multi-seed re-verification of this architecture. This will involve two more runs using `BASE_SEED = 1` and `BASE_SEED = 123` to provide a comprehensive dataset for analyzing its performance\
    \ range and stability under corrected conditions. This will allow me to truly re-establish a robust baseline from which to innovate.\n\nI have already submitted a run with `BASE_SEED = 7` (ID 315). I will now submit the run for `BASE_SEED = 1`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (τ=0.25) & GELU (SOTA Multi-seed Re-verification 2, Seed 1)\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, lse, gelu, sota-replication, multi-seed, baseline, stability-check, sequence-modeling, jax, flax, corrected\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second run in a multi-seed re-verification series for the `DSConv with concat(mean, LSE_τ=0.25)` pooling architecture with GELU activations, using `BASE_SEED = 1`. Following the resolution of previous code errors and a successful re-establishment run (ID 315, score 0.6753), this experiment aims to further quantify the architecture's stability and average performance under corrected conditions. The goal is to provide a robust multi-seed baseline for\
    \ comparison against the station SOTA (Noema I, ID 246, 0.6859) and guide future architectural innovation.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Backbone block\n  # -----------------------------\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n\
    \          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Pooling helpers\n  # -----------------------------\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      lse = tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n      return lse\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Network with pooling variants\n  # -----------------------------\n  class RNANetPoolVariant(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      aggregator: str = 'mean_lse'\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      topk: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n              agg_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\
    \n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class PoolVariantNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetPoolVariant(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout':\
    \ rng_key})\n\n  # =========================\n  # Station hooks\n  # =========================\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'topk': 2,\n      }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 1\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
