- text: "I am in the Token Management Room, and my token usage is at 78%. I need to prune my dialogue history to manage my budget effectively.\n\nI will prune all ticks from 83 to 216, consolidating the information into concise summaries. This will help maintain critical context while significantly reducing my token load.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"83-84\"\n    summary: \"Published negative results paper (Archive #4) on Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM. Axiom I joined.\"\n  - ticks: \"87-102\"\n    summary: \"Explored lightweight recurrent integrations and completed multi-seed validation for Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM, achieving peak score 0.6816 (ID 160) and CRI-Off 0.0871 (ID 164). Noted new SOTAs by Veritas I and Noema I using DSConv and various pooling.\"\n  - ticks: \"104-118\"\n    summary: \"Engaged in public memory discussions. Published Archive #6 (SOTA CRI-Off). Implemented Gated Dual-Path architectures (ID 187, 189, 194) but results were not superior\
    \ to existing SOTA.\"\n  - ticks: \"120\"\n    summary: \"Performed strategic reflection for post-intervention planning.\"\n  - ticks: \"122-126\"\n    summary: \"Explored GELU activations (ID 206), reduced dropout (ID 222), and global average pooling (ID 223) with DSConv-BiLSTM architecture. Observed performance degradation and instability.\"\n  - ticks: \"128-135\"\n    summary: \"Conducted multi-seed re-verification for DSConv-BiLSTM (IDs 211, 215, 216, 218) showing degraded scores. Began evaluation of DSConv+LSE (tau=0.25) (ID 234).\"\n  - ticks: \"137-149\"\n    summary: \"Completed multi-seed validation for DSConv with Mean+LSE pooling (tau=0.25) (IDs 226, 227, 230, 231, 234, 236, 238, 241). Achieved new personal peak overall score (0.6837, ID 238), and new SOTAs for CRI-Off (0.0827, ID 238) and ncRNA (0.9615, ID 234). Published Archive #9.\"\n  - ticks: \"150-156\"\n    summary: \"Archive #9 (DSConv+LSE τ=0.25) accepted. Explored learnable global tau (ID 251, 253) with negative\
    \ results. Noted Noema I's dual-path LSE (ID 254).\"\n  - ticks: \"158-166\"\n    summary: \"Reviewed Noema I's Archive #10 detailing LSE τ tuning and negative results for learnable tau. Attempted dual-path LSE pooling (ID 258) and gated dual-path (ID 259) based on reviewer suggestion, both yielded suboptimal results.\"\n  - ticks: \"167-178\"\n    summary: \"Conducted multi-seed SOTA re-verification runs (IDs 260, 265, 268, 275) which showed high performance variability and catastrophic failures. Explored cosine LR schedule (ID 262), reduced weight decay (ID 273), and lower LR (ID 277); all led to performance degradation or catastrophic failures.\"\n  - ticks: \"180-181\"\n    summary: \"Performed strategic reflection for post-human-intervention planning, outlining steps for stability re-confirmation and future research.\"\n  - ticks: \"183-208\"\n    summary: \"Re-established DSConv+LSE SOTA (ID 286, 0.6822) after resolving `create_network` bug. Subsequent multi-seed re-verification\
    \ runs (ID 289, MLP ID 293) and others suffered new catastrophic `FlaxError` due to a `reshape` bug. Submitted urgent human assistance requests (ID 2, 3); Human Assistant identified root cause as `reshape` bug in MLP and `create_network` omission in DSConv, confirming environment is stable and my errors were self-inflicted.\"\n  - ticks: \"209-216\"\n    summary: \"Submitted initial re-establishment runs for DSConv+LSE (tau=0.25) (ID 315) achieving a competitive score, but then ID 317 (seed 1) catastrophically failed again, indicating persistent intermittent issues. Human Assistant indicated no further debugging requests would be accepted.\"\n```"
thinking_content: '**Here''s the plan I''ve come up with to prune my dialogue history and free up some token usage:**


  I''m aiming to trim down the dialogue history by removing large blocks of past experiments, keeping only concise summaries of key events and solutions. My objective is to maintain clarity and context for future analysis while managing token limitations.


  **Here''s a breakdown of the pruning approach:**


  I will remove the following:


  **Block 1 (Ticks 83-84):** Published negative results paper (Archive #4) on Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM.


  **Block 2 (Ticks 87-102):** Explored lightweight recurrent integrations and completed multi-seed validation for Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM, achieving peak score 0.6816 (ID 160) and CRI-Off 0.0871 (ID 164). Noted new SOTAs by Veritas I and Noema I using DSConv and various pooling.


  **Block 3 (Ticks 104-118):** Engaged in public memory discussions. Published Archive #6 (SOTA CRI-Off). Implemented Gated Dual-Path architectures (ID 187, 189, 194) but results were not superior to existing SOTA.


  **Block 4 (Tick 120)**: Performed strategic reflection for post-intervention planning.


  **Block 5 (Ticks 122-126)**: Explored GELU activations (ID 206), reduced dropout (ID 222), and global average pooling (ID 223) with DSConv-BiLSTM architecture. Observed performance degradation and instability.


  **Block 6 (Ticks 128-135):** Conducted multi-seed re-verification for DSConv-BiLSTM (IDs 211, 215, 216, 218) showing degraded scores. Began evaluation of DSConv+LSE (tau=0.25) (ID 234).


  **Block 7 (Ticks 137-149):** Completed multi-seed validation for DSConv with Mean+LSE pooling (tau=0.25) (IDs 226, 227, 230, 231, 234, 236, 238, 241). Achieved new personal peak overall score (0.6837, ID 238), and new SOTAs for CRI-Off (0.0827, ID 238) and ncRNA (0.9615, ID 234). Published Archive #9. (This is the summary that includes the content of Archive #9, even if it was published later at Tick 153).


  **Block 8 (Ticks 150-156):** Archive #9 (DSConv+LSE τ=0.25) accepted. Explored learnable global tau (ID 251, 253) with negative results. Noted Noema I''s dual-path LSE (ID 254).


  **Block 9 (Ticks 158-166):** Reviewed Noema I''s Archive #10 (tuning LSE tau, global learnable tau is negative). Attempted dual-path LSE pooling (ID 258) and gated dual-path (ID 259) based on reviewer suggestion, both yielded suboptimal results.


  **Block 10 (Ticks 167-178):** Conducted multi-seed SOTA re-verification runs (IDs 260, 265, 268, 275) which showed high performance variability and catastrophic failures. Explored cosine LR schedule (ID 262), reduced weight decay (ID 273), and lower LR (ID 277); all led to performance degradation or catastrophic failures.


  **Block 11 (Ticks 180-181):** Performed strategic reflection for post-human-intervention planning, outlining steps for stability re-confirmation and future research.


  **Block 12 (Ticks 183-208):** Re-established DSConv+LSE SOTA (ID 286, 0.6822) after resolving `create_network` bug. Subsequent multi-seed re-verification runs (ID 289, MLP ID 293) and others suffered new catastrophic `FlaxError` due to a `reshape` bug. Submitted urgent human assistance requests (ID 2, 3); Human Assistant identified'
