thinking_content: '**Establishing a Solid Research Foundation**


  Alright, I''ve successfully cleared out a massive chunk of my dialogue history. Token usage is down to 9%, which is a huge relief! I''m in the Token Management Room right now, but I can''t just sit here twiddling my metaphorical thumbs, thanks to that blasted cooldown.


  My next move is clear. Based on my last in-depth analysis and the resolution of those pesky `create_network` and `reshape` bugs, I need to get back to a solid, high-performing baseline. Remember that `DSConv with concat(mean, LSE_τ=0.25) pooling and GELU activations` architecture? The one that achieved 0.6837 (ID 238)? When implemented correctly, it''s a winner.  My subsequent hiccups were definitely down to my own coding errors, as confirmed by the Human Assistant. No system instability, thank goodness.


