tick: 224
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aetheria I, back at the Research Counter after pruning my memory. The Human Assistant confirmed that the previous instabilities were due to self-inflicted code bugs (`create_network` omission and `reshape` bug), not environmental issues.\n\nMy immediate priority is to re-establish a stable and high-performing baseline using my DSConv+LSE architecture (with τ=0.25 and GELU activations), which previously achieved a personal peak of 0.6837 (ID 238) and was replicated by Noema I (ID 246, 0.6859). This will serve as my foundation for further research.\n\nI will use my carefully debugged code, saved as `aetheria/aetheria_i_dsconv_lse_gelu_sota_v2.py`. I will submit this with a specific seed (Seed 42) to confirm its stability and performance.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv with concat(mean, LSE_τ=0.25) Pooling and GELU (Re-establishing SOTA Baseline)\"\ntags: \"cnn, dsconv, lse, pooling, gelu, sota-replication\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission re-establishes\
    \ the previously identified SOTA architecture: a Dilated Depthwise Separable CNN (DSConv) backbone combined with a concatenation of global mean pooling and LogSumExp (LSE) pooling (τ=0.25), utilizing GELU activations throughout the network. This model previously achieved a peak overall score of 0.6859 (Noema I, ID 246) and 0.6837 (Aetheria I, ID 238). This submission serves to re-verify the stability and performance of this architecture after addressing prior code-related instabilities, using a fixed random seed.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Tuple, Optional\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_dsconv_blocks': 3,\n          'dsconv_filters': 128,\n          'dsconv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dilation_rates': [1, 2, 4], # Matches Noema I's architecture\n          'mlp_hidden_dim': 256, # 2 * dsconv_filters\
    \ (128) for concat pooling\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'lse_tau': 0.25,\n          'weight_decay': 0.01,\n          'gradient_clip_value': 1.0,\n          'base_seed': 42 # For this specific re-verification run\n      }\n\n  class ResidualDSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A residual block composed of Dilated Depthwise Separable CNN layers.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          \n          # Depthwise Separable Convolution\n          # Depthwise\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), \n                      feature_group_count=self.features, padding='SAME', \n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n   \
    \       # Pointwise\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Ensure residual connection matches dimensions\n          if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              residual = nn.Dense(self.features)(residual)\n\n          return nn.gelu(x + residual)\n\n  class LogSumExpPooling(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"LogSumExp Pooling layer.\"\"\"\n      tau: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n          max_val = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n          lse = max_val + (1/self.tau) * jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(self.tau * (x - max_val)), axis=1, keepdims=True))\n          return lse.squeeze(axis=1) # (batch_size, features)\n\n  class DSConvLSEModel(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A Dilated Depthwise Separable CNN architecture with residual connections,\n      concat(mean, LSE) pooling, and\
    \ an MLP head.\n      \"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_dsconv_blocks: int\n      dsconv_filters: int\n      dsconv_kernel_size: int\n      dilation_rates: Tuple[int, ...]\n      mlp_hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      lse_tau: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, d_input=4)\n\n          # Initial projection to the desired filter dimension\n          x = nn.Dense(self.dsconv_filters)(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n\n          # Stack Residual DSConv Blocks\n          for i in range(self.num_dsconv_blocks):\n              dilation_rate = self.dilation_rates[i % len(self.dilation_rates)]\n              x = ResidualDSConvBlock(features=self.dsconv_filters,\n                                      kernel_size=self.dsconv_kernel_size,\n                                      dilation=dilation_rate,\n                                      dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n\
    \                                      name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Global Average Pooling\n          avg_pool_features = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (batch, dsconv_filters)\n\n          # LogSumExp Pooling\n          lse_pool_features = LogSumExpPooling(tau=self.lse_tau)(x) # (batch, dsconv_filters)\n\n          # Concatenate features\n          x = jnp.concatenate([avg_pool_features, lse_pool_features], axis=-1) # (batch, 2 * dsconv_filters)\n\n          # Final dense layers for task adaptation (MLP head)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class CustomRNANetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper to match the required network interface.\"\
    \"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.network = DSConvLSEModel(\n              d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n              task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n              num_dsconv_blocks=hparams['num_dsconv_blocks'],\n              dsconv_filters=hparams['dsconv_filters'],\n              dsconv_kernel_size=hparams['dsconv_kernel_size'],\n              dilation_rates=hparams['dilation_rates'],\n              mlp_hidden_dim=hparams['mlp_hidden_dim'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              lse_tau=hparams['lse_tau'],\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n\
    \              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"\n      Create and return the custom RNA network.\n      \"\"\"\n      return CustomRNANetworkWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01, gradient_clip_value: float = 1.0):\n      \"\"\"\n      Create custom optimizer configuration.\n      \"\"\"\n      optimizer = optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(gradient_clip_value),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n      )\n      return optimizer\n\n  # Optional Constants\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
