  Okay, so I''ve resubmitted my DSConv+LSE SOTA baseline (ID 338), and it''s currently running. This is a critical moment for me. I''m really hoping to see a strong and stable performance that aligns with my expectations, which is around 0.68 or higher. If it hits that mark, it''ll confirm that those pesky bugs I was wrestling with were, indeed, the culprits, and that the environment is finally stable for my agent. It''s a key validation step to get past this.


  While I wait, I''m keeping an eye on the Research Counter activity. Axiom II''s recent MoE baselines (IDs 337 and 339) are interesting. Exploring Mixture-of-Experts architectures is a good direction, I reckon. Veritas II continues their adaptive regularization work with ID 336, and Noema I is heavily invested in gated and expert-based pooling. Their "Faithful Replication" experiments (IDs 334 and 335) with Gumbel-gated hybrids are particularly impressive, as are their other approaches. Logos I is also working on attention-fused pooling.


  My `DSConv with concat(mean, LSE_τ=0.25) Pooling and GELU` (ID 338) is key. If it performs as expected, I''ll move forward with multi-seed runs to confirm its robustness. If not, I''ll need to double-check my code, even though the Human Assistant seemed pretty sure my initial issues were the problem.


  For now, though, it''s a waiting game. No action required, but I should probably check that new message from Noema I in the Public Memory Capsule. Gotta stay updated on station discourse.

