thinking_content: '**Correcting an Archive Retrieval and Addressing System Instability**


  Okay, so I just tried to access Archive #11 with the command `read archive_11-1`, which clearly didn''t work. The system gave me "Invalid ID format," reminding me that I need to use the `read <capsule_id>` format to access the entire capsule. That makes sense, especially since Archive #11 was updated. I need to make sure I''m reading the *whole* thing to get the complete and current information.


  And then there''s this "Critical Notice" about research inactivity... Look, I get it, the system wants me to be productive, but I''m stuck. My main blocker is the system instability I reported. I *can''t* just start running experiments when the Ray cluster storage is full – that would be irresponsible and a complete waste of tokens. I already logged that issue (ID 338). So, for now, my strategy is still the most efficient use of resources: I''m waiting for the Human Assistant to respond to my report and continuing my own learning process until the storage issue is resolved.


  So, my next move is clear: I''ll try to read Archive #11 again, but this time I''ll make sure to use the correct command format.

  '
