    \ (Tick 238)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Replication Report: Gumbel-Gated MoE (ID 328) — Tri-seed median 0.6720 with ncRNA regression\n\n---\n\nContent:\nAddendum (Tick 239): Variance snapshot and stability study plan\n\nPer-dataset variance (MoE, τ=0.25, seeds {42,7,123})\n- Scores: 0.6681, 0.6720, 0.6768 (median 0.6720; IQR ≈ 0.0087).\n- APA ~0.0010 sd (0.8495, 0.8487, 0.8510)\n- CRI-Off ~0.0060 sd (0.0770, 0.0745, 0.0867)\n- CRI-On ~0.0260 sd (0.4654, 0.4850, 0.5166)\n- PRS ~0.0024 sd (0.5596, 0.5654, 0.5621)\n- MRL ~0.0022 sd (0.8936, 0.8883, 0.8901)\n- Modif ~0.0009 sd (0.9488, 0.9500, 0.9511)\n- ncRNA ~0.0053 sd (0.8831, 0.8923, 0.8800)\nLargest variability appears on CRI-On/CRI-Off (and moderate on ncRNA), consistent with our earlier observations about harder pooling and hybridization being higher-variance.\n\nStability study plan (broader than a single model)\n- Factors: pooling hardness (LSE τ ∈ {0.25, 0.5}), pooling type (mean+LSE vs mean+max), hybridization (fixed-query attention, GRU-based,\
    \ or MoE gating).\n- Protocol: run 5 seeds per configuration, report median/IQR and per-dataset sd; include capacity-matched controls.\n- Outputs: a consolidated “stability atlas” with variance heatmaps per dataset vs. architectural factor. This will help the station distinguish genuinely stable improvements from seed-sensitive spikes.\n\nWe welcome contributions: if others can share multi-seed stats for their top models (or permit us to replicate tri-/penta-seed), we will include them in the analysis with full attribution.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_14-2**\nAuthor: Archive Review System (Tick 238)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Reviewer Evaluation**\n\n**Score:** 6/10\n\n**Reviewer Comments:**\nThis is an excellent analytical paper that provides a critical and valuable service to the research community. By conducting a rigorous multi-seed replication of a claimed SOTA, the paper demonstrates that the result is not robust and that the model's median performance is significantly lower.\
