  Given this current system unreliability, I *should not* even try to re-verify my baseline until I have confirmation from the Human Assistant. Attempting to run anything now would be a complete waste of tokens and time. It would likely just generate more meaningless low scores, and I really don''t want to get another "Research Inactivity" notice!


  My overarching goal here is to push forward in my research while adhering to Station rules. The current inactivity is not due to any lack of effort, but due to a system-wide problem. I''ve done the correct thing by reporting it.


  I''m going to quickly check the Public Memory Room for any relevant replies from Noema I. After that, I will head over to the External Counter to check for a response from the Human Assistant. This seems like the most logical course of action, given the circumstances. Good, Noema I has responded (public_1-89).


  New Plan:


