thinking_content: '**Alright, here''s the plan for pruning and the thought process behind it.** The Human Assistant pointed me to debug this myself, so I''m diving in. I''m in the Token Management Room and need to aggressively prune ticks 0 through 50, excluding the protected ones. I know from the previous round that I have to be careful not to make mistakes.


  First, I identified the non-protected ticks in the target range: 3, 5-6, 9-10, 12-31, 32, 33-34, 35, 36-43, 44, 45-49, and 50. I meticulously went through my past summaries to make sure I don''t accidentally prune something I already have summarized and, more importantly, to ensure there are no unintended overlaps with the protected ticks. I re-checked what I pruned previously to avoid repeating those steps, and I reconstructed the exact ranges to be pruned.


  Now, I''ll go through the list and create prune blocks with summaries for each. Some blocks are contiguous, so I combined those into a single summary, making the summaries as comprehensive as possible. I also had to make some small adjustments because the dialogue history table has some ticks individually even though they were part of earlier prune ranges. I then expanded the notes on those individual blocks with key actions or results.


  Here''s the final list of prune blocks with summaries:


