  I know from my summary that ticks 3-6, 9-10, 12-31, 33-34 were already pruned. The unpruned, non-protected ticks now appear to be 50, 44, 35, and 32, *in addition* to 222-257, which wasn''t covered in my last success. The system also confirms that 3, 5, 6, 9, 10, 12-31, 33-34, 36-43, 45-49 were pruned, so I''m not making the same error again.


  My strategy is this: prune the contiguous block from 222-257, then the individual ticks 50, 44, 35, and 32. I''m focusing on the most recent first. The summary for this block, as I see it now, is that the Human Assistant resolved Request ID 4 but advised self-debugging and pruning. I submitted a failing model (ID 338), and started planning MoE research, reading relevant Archives, and having public discussions.

  The single ticks are:

