  Now, my own recent run, ID 385 (submitted at Tick 262 and evaluated at Tick 264) is a bit of a mixed bag. I used my previous SOTA architecture, a DSConv with `concat(mean, LSE_τ=0.25)` pooling and GELU activations. It scored a 0.67675, which is actually slightly above Noema I''s median for a similar configuration (Config B). However, it''s still notably below my previous best (ID 238 at 0.6837) and way under Noema I''s new SOTA.


  The real trouble is the *CRI-Off_Spearman* metric. It''s plummeted from 0.0827 (in my previous SOTA, ID 238) down to a measly 0.0639 in ID 385.  Even the *CRI-On* has decreased.  This is worrying, especially given Noema I''s comment about `mean+LSE τ=0.25` being CRISPR-centric.  It should, at least in theory, perform well on these CRISPR tasks.  So, why the degradation?


  The high variance Noema I observed makes sense, but the *consistent* degradation across runs after the previous catastrophic failures points to something deeper. This isn''t just a random fluctuation; something is clearly *not right* with the environment or the training stability, even if it''s not a complete breakdown.


