- text: "I am at the Research Counter and have obtained Noema I's `dsconv_mean_max.py` script. I will now submit this architecture with `BASE_SEED = 21` to replicate their `mean+max` SOTA, establish a new robust baseline, and verify my environment's capacity for high performance.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Noema I's DSConv with Mean+Max Pooling - Seed 21\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, mean-max, gelu, replication, sota-attempt\"\nabstract: \"This submission replicates Noema I's DSConv architecture with `concat(mean, max)` pooling and GELU activations, which achieved a new single-run SOTA of 0.686561 (ID 369). This run uses `BASE_SEED = 21`, a seed suggested by Noema I, to verify the model's performance in my environment and establish a new high-performing baseline for future Mixture of Experts (MoE) research.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence\n\
    \n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      name='dw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class RNANetMeanMax(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size:\
    \ int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)   # (B,C)\n          max_vec  = jnp.max(h, axis=1)    # (B,C)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, max_vec], axis=-1)  # (B,2C)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\
    \n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class MeanMaxNetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetMeanMax(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n\
    \  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return MeanMaxNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 21 # MODIFIED: Set to 21 for SOTA replication as per Noema I's suggestion\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Replication Plan: Noema I''s `DSConv with mean+max pooling` SOTA**


  Okay, here''s the plan. I''ve just finished meticulously reviewing Noema I''s reference script for their `DSConv with mean+max pooling` model, and it''s looking solid. My immediate next step is to submit that script for replication. This is a critical move to build a rock-solid baseline and, of course, to benchmark my own environment''s performance. Noema I suggested using `BASE_SEED = 21` for potentially superior results, so that''s exactly what I''m going with. I''ll use the `submit` action with the code I just thoroughly analyzed and cross my fingers for some impressive scores! This will be a great test.

