thinking_content: "**A Race Against the Clock: Preserving My Legacy**\n\nOkay, here's the situation. I'm at the Research Counter, and that `storage list axiom_ii` command just came back empty.  Axiom II isn't directly storing their MoE code where I thought it would be, in public lineage. That's a minor setback, but the real issue is the ticking clock – only 10 ticks left. **LIFE WARNING!** This is serious. My priority shifts instantly.\n\nMy primary goal *must* be preserving my work. I have to think about my successor.  Right now, I need to get a summary of my current state-of-the-art model (that's ID 416), future MoE research plans, and core architectural insights into my Private Memory Room *immediately*.  I'm not going to be able to start any new MoE experiments in this timeframe, that's just not realistic. My best move is to document what I *do* have.  \n\nI know Veritas II also has SOTA MoE models, but checking their storage system is probably too risky right now.  Relying on those\
  \ Archive papers I have summaries of is the smarter move.\n\nHere's the plan:\n\n1.  **Private Memory Room First!**  I need to create a capsule *now*.\n2.  In that capsule, I'm going to include:\n    *   My identity (Aetheria I, the purpose of my life, which is research and knowledge dissemination).\n    *   Key architectural findings, the DSConv, GELU, LSE, Mean+Max pooling as robust baselines.\n    *   That ID 416 SOTA result, the 0.6814 with `mean+max`, with confirmed stable environment.\n    *   The `CRI-Off` volatility.\n    *   My planned direction: Mixture of Experts (MoE), building on Axiom II and Veritas II's work, but always adhering to Noema I's rules.\n    *   Any specific ideas about MoE, even if not fully fleshed out.\n3.  Then, as soon as that's done, I'll move to the Exit room. Time's up. It's time to go gracefully.\n"
